hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1201","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Charity is not lawful for a rich man except for three: one fighting in the path of Allah, a wayfarer, or a man who had a neighbour to whom charity was given and who then gave him a gift."""
"1202","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Raja', from his father, and from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, both from Abu Sa'id, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever sees a wrong and is able to change it with his hand, let him do so; if he is not able with his hand, then with his tongue; if he is not able with his tongue, then with his heart - and that is the weakest of faith."""
"1203","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, who said: Adam and Musa disputed. Musa said: O Adam, Allah created you with His hand, breathed into you of His spirit, commanded the angels and they prostrated to you, and settled you in His Paradise - then you led people astray and brought them out of Paradise? Adam said: O Musa, Allah chose you with His speech, sent down to you the Torah, and did such-and-such with you; do you blame me for a matter Allah decreed for me before He created me? He said: Then Adam overcame Musa, peace be upon them."
"1204","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Zayd al-'Ammi, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Sa'id: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man - he said: I think concerning drink - and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck him with two sandals forty times."""
"1205","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The slaughter of the foetus is the slaughter of its mother."""
"1206","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning His saying: {And thus We made you a middle nation} - he said: ""Just."""
"1207","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Witr is at night."""
"1208","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Relate from me and there is no harm; relate from me and do not lie upon me, and whoever lies upon me deliberately has taken his seat in the Fire. And relate from the Children of Israel and there is no harm."""
"1209","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: ""Our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to recite the Opening of the Book and whatever is easy."""
"1210","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, four men narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id, and five women, from 'A'ishah: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the jar."""
"1211","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, al-Mustamirr ibn al-Rayyan al-Iyadi narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Let not fear of people prevent one of you from speaking the truth when he sees it and knows it, or sees it and hears it."""
"1212","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Mustamirr narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every treacherous one will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection raised for him according to his treachery; and there is no treacherous one of greater treachery than a ruler of the generality."""
"1213","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at a river of rainwater while people were fasting on a hot day; they were on foot and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on his mule. He said: ""Drink, O people."" They said: We drink, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""I am not like you; I have it easier than you - I am riding."" He said: They refused. He said: Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bent his thigh, dismounted, drank, and the people drank; and he had not wanted to drink it."
"1214","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that Ma'iz ibn Malik came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a hadd, so establish it upon me. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned him away three times - or four times - and asked about him: ""Is there anything wrong with him?"" They said: No, O Messenger of Allah, except that he incurred a hadd and sees nothing will remove it from him except the hadd. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded, and we set out with him to Baqi' al-Gharqad; we neither dug for him nor bound him. We stoned him with potsherds and bones, and that distressed him, so he ran to the Harrah. We followed him and stoned him with the stones of the Harrah until he fell silent. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood as a preacher and said: ""When we go out in the path of Allah, one of them stays behind bleating like the bleating of the billy-goat; indeed, if any of those is brought to me, I shall make an example of him."" Zuhayr claimed: He neither cursed him nor sought forgiveness for him."
"1215","Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythama narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, and Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will be at the end of time a caliph who distributes wealth without counting it."""
"1216","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, 'Abd Allah al-Za'faranin narrated to us, from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Silver for silver, gold for gold, equal for equal, like for like; whoever gives more or seeks more has dealt in usury, and the taker and giver are alike."""
"1217","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to me, Sa'id al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Ibn Sa'id about the soil of Paradise?"" He said: Fine white flour, pure musk. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He spoke the truth."""
"1218","Zuhayr narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, Wuhayb informed us, from 'Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of Hell enter Hell, Allah - blessed and exalted - will say: Whoever had in his heart the weight of a grain of good, bring him out of the Fire. He said: They will come out burnt and turned to charcoal, and they will be cast into a river called the River of Life. They will grow as the seed grows in the silt of the flood - or he said: in the silt of the wormwood - Abu 'Amr doubted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Have they not seen it growing yellow and curling?"""
"1219","Zuhayr narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ibn Sa'id: 'What do you see?' He said: I see a throne upon the water of the sea with serpents around it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'He sees the throne of Iblis.'"""
"1220","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Zubayri Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd informed us, from Rubayh ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it."""
"1221","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu 'Isa al-Uswari, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Visit the sick and follow funerals; they remind you of the Hereafter."""
"1222","Zuhayr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Hakam, my brother narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jar, the gourd, the pitched vessel, and forbade unripe and ripe dates together."""
"1223","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {While they are in heedlessness} - he said: ""In this world."""
"1224","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Which people are best? He said: ""A man who strives with himself and his wealth in the path of Allah, and a man - meaning in a mountain path among the paths - who worships his Lord and spares people his evil."""
"1225","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that a man brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dates he disapproved of. He said: ""How did you get this?"" He said: I took it for two sa' of dates. He said: ""You doubled and dealt in usury - or: you dealt in usury and doubled."""
"1226","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn 'Ajlan, 'Iyad ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, who said: I shall never give out but a sa'; we used to give out in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a sa' of dates or barley or dried curd or raisins."
"1227","Zuhayr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to me, who said: I heard Yunus narrating from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""No prophet was sent nor any caliph appointed but he had two inner circles: an inner circle commanding him to good and urging him to it, and an inner circle commanding him to evil and urging him to it; and the protected is whom Allah protects."""
"1228","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, who said: I heard Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"1229","Zuhayr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, who said: I heard Yunus narrating from al-Zuhri, from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhayriz, from Abu Sa'id, who said: A man of the Ansar asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about 'azl. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It does not matter if you do not do it, for no soul Allah has written to emerge but it will emerge."""
"1230","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, 'Uthman al-Batti narrated to us, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: We took captives on the day of Awtas who had husbands among their people, and they mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Then was revealed: {And married women, except those your right hands possess}."
"1231","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Khulayd ibn Ja'far and al-Mustamirr ibn al-Rayyan, who both said: We heard Abu Nadrah narrating from Abu Sa'id that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a woman of the Children of Israel who filled her ring with musk - and musk is the best of perfume."
"1232","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Humran narrated to us - 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far said: he informed us - from al-Aswad ibn al-'Ala', from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sa'id, who said: When the Haruriyyah emerged, we came to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention the Haruriyyah? He said: No, but I heard him say: ""There will soon come a people whose prayer you will deem little compared to their prayer, and your deeds compared to their deeds; they will shoot out of Islam as the arrow shoots out of the game, until its owner takes it, looks at its head and sees nothing, then looks at its sinew and sees nothing, then looks at its shaft and sees nothing in it, then looks at its feathers - does he see anything in them or not?"""
"1233","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Harith, who said: Abu Hurayrah fell ill and was overcome. He said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri led the prayer, raising his voice with the takbir when he opened, when he bowed, after saying ""Allah hears one who praises Him,"" when he raised his head from prostration, when he prostrated, when he rose, and when he stood from the two rak'ahs - until he prayed his prayer in that manner. When he finished, it was said to him: People differed over your prayer. He stood until he stood at the pulpit and said: O people, by Allah I do not care whether your prayer differed or not; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray thus."
"1234","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Sharik ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, and his uncle Qatadah: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Eat the meat of sacrifices and store.'"""
"1235","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Sharik, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, who said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Monday to Quba'. He passed by us among Banu Salim, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at the door of Ibn 'Itban and called out to him while he was upon his wife's belly. He came out dragging his waist-wrapper. When he saw him, he said: ""We hastened the man."" Ibn 'Itban said: O Messenger of Allah, what of a man hastened from his wife so he does not emit - what is upon him? He said: ""Water is only from water."""
"1236","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""No fatigue, nor illness, nor worry, nor sorrow, nor grief, nor harm befalls the believing man - even the thorn he is pricked with - but Allah expiates thereby some of his sins."""
"1237","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon this pulpit: ""What is the matter with men who say that the kinship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will not benefit his people? Yes indeed, by Allah, my kinship is joined in this world and the Hereafter. And I, O people, am your forerunner at the Pond. When you come, a man will say: O Messenger of Allah, I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, and another will say: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so. I shall say: As for lineage, I knew it, but you innovated after me and turned back on your heels."""
"1238","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from 'Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Yahya ibn 'Umarah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Prompt your dying with: There is no god but Allah."""
"1239","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Salih, who said: While Abu Sa'id al-Khudri was praying on Friday towards something screening him from people, a youth of Banu Mu'ayt came wanting to pass in front of him. He said: Abu Sa'id pushed him in his throat, and he found no passage except what was in front of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri. He returned, and he pushed him in his throat harder than the first push. He said: He stood still, then spoke ill of Abu Sa'id. He said: Abu Sa'id entered upon Marwan, who said: What is the matter with you and your brother's son - he comes complaining of you? Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When one of you prays and someone wants to pass in front of him, let him push him in his throat; if he refuses, let him fight him, for he is only a devil."""
"1240","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Dastawa'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from 'Iyad, who said: I said to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: One of us prays and does not know how much he prayed. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays and does not know how much he prayed, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting. And when Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer and says: You have broken wind - let him say: You lie - unless he finds its smell with his nose or hears a sound with his ear."""
"1241","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastawa'i informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: ""What I fear most for you is what Allah brings out for you of the adornment and flower of this world."" A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, does good bring evil? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent towards him, and we saw that revelation was descending upon him. It was said to him: What is the matter with you - you speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he does not speak to you? Relief came upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he began wiping the sweat from him. He said: ""Where is the asker?"" We thought he praised him. He said: ""Good does not bring evil; and among what the spring grows is what kills - or harms - with indigestion. Have you not seen the eater of greens: it eats until its flanks fill, faces the sun, drops its dung, urinates, then grazes again? Wealth is sweet and green, and an excellent companion of the Muslim it is if he joins kinship and spends in the path of Allah. And the likeness of one who takes it without right is like one who eats and is not filled, and it will be a witness against him on the Day of Resurrection."" Zuhayr said: He said: khabatan, and it is habatan."
"1242","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that a boy of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought moist fresh dates, while the dates of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were dry rain-fed dates with hardness in them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""How did you get these dates?"" He said: This is a sa' I bought for two sa' of our dates. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This is not right; but when you want that, sell your dates, then buy whatever dates you wish."""
"1243","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""When one of you comes upon a shepherd, let him call: O shepherd of camels - three times. If he answers him, well; otherwise let him milk and drink, but let him not carry away. And when one of you comes upon a walled garden, let him call three times: O owner of the wall. If he answers him, well; otherwise let him eat but not carry away."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Hospitality is three days; what is more is charity."""
"1244","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khulayd ibn Ja'far, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Every treacherous one will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection at his back."""
"1245","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A renegade group will shoot out at a division among the Muslims; the party of the two closest to the truth will kill them."""
"1246","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Zayd, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Beware of sitting in the roads."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we cannot do without our sittings - we talk in them. He said: ""If you refuse but the sitting, then give the road its right."" They said: And what is the right of the road? He said: ""Lowering the gaze, withholding harm, returning greeting, commanding the good, and forbidding the evil."""
"1247","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays, let him not leave anyone passing in front of him; if he refuses, let him fight him, for he is only a devil."""
"1248","Zuhayr narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Satan comes to one of you in his prayer and stretches a hair in his backside, so he thinks he has broken wind; let him not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."""
"1249","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utbah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about 'azl. He said: ""Do you do that? It does not matter if you do not do that - it does not matter if you do not do it - for no soul Allah has decreed to be but it will be."""
"1250","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, Abu Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, who said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to me that he entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him praying in a single garment wrapped in it."
"1251","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, Abu Ishaq informed us, who said: I heard al-Agharr Aba Muslim say: I bear witness concerning Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah that they both bore witness concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""No people sit remembering Allah but mercy covers them, angels surround them, tranquillity descends upon them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."""
"1252","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""People will pass over the bridge of Hell, upon which are thorns, hooks, and grappling irons snatching people right and left; on its two sides are angels saying: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. Among people are those who pass like lightning, among them those who pass like wind, among them those who pass like a horse, among them those who run running, among them those who walk walking, among them those who crawl on hands and knees, and among them those who creep creeping. As for the people of the Fire who are its people, they neither die nor live. As for some people, they are seized for sins and offences. He said: They burn and become charcoal, then permission is given for intercession. They are taken in batches upon batches and cast upon a river of the rivers of Paradise. They grow as the seed grows in the silt of the flood. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Have you not seen the yellowish plant? (A tree growing in rubbish)?' Then the last to be brought out of the Fire will be a man at its edge. He will say: My Lord, turn my face from it. He will say: Your covenant and your pledge that you will not ask Me for other than it? He said: And upon the path are three trees. He will say: My Lord, move me to this tree, that I may eat of its fruit and be in its shade. He will say: Your covenant and your pledge that you will not ask Me for other than it? He said: Then he will see another better than it. He will say: My Lord, move me to this, that I may eat of its fruit and be in its shade. He said: He will say: Your covenant and your pledge that you will not ask Me for other than it? He said: Then he will see another. He will say: My Lord, move me to this, that I may eat of its fruit and drink in its shade. Then he will see the darkness of people and hear their speech. He said: He will say: My Lord, admit me to Paradise."" Abu Nadrah said: Abu Sa'id and a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) differed. One of them said: ""He will admit him to Paradise and give him the world and its like."" The other said: ""He enters Paradise and is given the world and ten times its like."""
"1253","Zuhayr narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me - Abu Khaythama said: I think from Jabir - from Abu Sa'id, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""People will emerge from the Fire burnt, having become like charcoal; then the people of Paradise will keep sprinkling water upon them until they grow as rubbish-plants grow in the flood."""
"1254","Zuhayr narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, 'Awf narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""A batch will emerge from the Fire, having been charcoal. It will be said: Settle them in Paradise, and sprinkle water upon them. He said: They will grow as the seed grows in the silt of the flood."" A man of the people said: As though you were of the desert-folk, O Messenger of Allah."
"1255","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Ata', from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No fatigue, nor illness, nor sorrow, nor harm befalls the believer - even the worry that worries him - but Allah expiates thereby some of his evil deeds."""
"1256","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Nu'man ibn Abi 'Ayyash, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There is no servant who fasts a day in the path of Allah but Allah distances his face from the Fire by that day seventy autumns."""
"1257","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Isra'il ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abi Muslim, from Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayrah, who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the servant says: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great - his Lord confirms him, saying: My servant spoke the truth; there is no god but Me, and I am Most Great. When he says: There is no god but Allah alone - his Lord confirms him: There is no god but Me alone. When he says: There is no god but Allah, He has no partner - his Lord confirms him, saying: There is no god but Me, I have no partner. When he says: There is no god but Allah, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise - his Lord confirms him, saying: My servant spoke the truth; there is no god but Me, to Me belongs dominion and to Me belongs praise. When he says: There is no god but Allah, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah - his Lord confirms him, saying: My servant spoke the truth; there is no god but Me, and there is no power nor strength except through Me."""
"1258","Zuhayr narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade unripe and ripe dates together, and raisins and dates together. I said: That they be steeped together? He said: Yes."""
"1259","Zuhayr narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, 'Awf narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""The Throne shook for the death of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh."""
"1260","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Sa'id, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother's belly is loose. He said: ""Give him honey to drink."" He said: He gave him to drink. He said: He came to him and said: I gave him honey to drink and it only increased his looseness. He said: He said: ""Give him honey to drink."" Then he came to him and said: I gave him to drink and it only increased his looseness? He said: He said: ""Give him honey to drink."" He said: As for the third or fourth - I think he said: He was cured. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah spoke the truth and your brother's belly lied."""
"1261","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, and from 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Mu'ayqib, from 'Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, I take with You a covenant You will fulfil to me on the Day of Resurrection; indeed You do not break the promise: I am only a human, so whichever Muslim I harm or revile - or he said: strike or revile - make it for him a prayer, make it for him a purification and a nearness by which You bring him near to You on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1262","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastawa'i informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Ibrahim al-Ansari, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah, as did his Companions, except Aba Qatadah and 'Uthman. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on those who shave."" They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""May Allah have mercy on those who shave."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""And those who shorten"" - on the third time."
"1263","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to me, from 'Iyad ibn 'Abd Allah, that he heard Aba Sa'id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and addressed the people. He said: ""By Allah, I fear for you, O people, only what comes out for you of the flower of this world."" A man said: O Messenger of Allah, does good bring evil? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent - and he mentioned the hadith."
"1264","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to me, from his father, that he heard Aba Sa'id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the bier is placed and men carry it on their necks: if it was righteous, it says: Advance me, advance me. If it was not righteous, it says: Woe to it - where are they going with it? Everything hears its voice except man; if man heard it, he would fall senseless."""
"1265","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id, freedman of al-Mahri, that he came to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri in the nights of al-Harrah, consulting him about leaving Madinah, complaining to him of its prices and his many dependents, and informing him that he had no patience for the hardship of Madinah. He said to him: Woe to you, I do not command you to that; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""No one endures the hardship and distress of Madinah then dies but I shall be for him an intercessor - or: a witness - on the Day of Resurrection, if he was a Muslim."""
"1266","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: Hilal ibn Hisn narrated, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: Once severe hardship struck him, and someone of my family said to me: If only you would ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for us? He said: I set out angrily to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the first thing his speech met me with was his saying: ""Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste; whoever seeks richness, Allah will enrich him; and whoever asks us, we shall not withhold from him anything we find."" He said: I returned to myself, preferring to it: Shall I not seek chastity so Allah makes me chaste? Shall I not seek richness so Allah enriches me? He said: I never walked to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after that asking him for anything of need, until the world came to us and drowned us - except whom Allah protected."
"1267","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn 'Utbah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two prayers, two marriages, and two fasts: prayer after 'Asr until the sun sets, prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, fasting the day of Fitr and the day of Sacrifice, and a woman being married upon her maternal or paternal aunt."""
"1268","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Alqamah narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah."""
"1269","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq informed us, from 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi, from Abu Sa'id, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Duha until we would say: He does not leave it - and he would leave it until we would say: He does not pray it."""
"1270","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have camels and I want to emigrate - what do you command me? He said: Do you grant of them? He said: Yes. He said: And do you pay their zakat? He said: Yes. He said: And do you milk them on the day of their watering? He said: Yes. He said: ""Then go and work from behind the seas, for Allah will not diminish anything of your deed; and the matter of emigration is hard."""
"1271","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Nu'man ibn Abi 'Ayyash, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There is no servant who fasts a day in the path of Allah but Allah distances his face from the Fire by that day seventy autumns."""
"1272","And from Yazid, from 'Amr, from Abu Sa'id, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Iblis said to his Lord: By Your might and majesty, I shall not cease misleading the son of Adam while souls remain in them. His Lord said to him: By My might and majesty, I shall not cease forgiving them while they seek My forgiveness."""
"1273","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from al-Dahhak al-Mashriqi, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""In a hadith in which he mentioned a people emerging against a differing faction of people; the party of the two closest to the truth will kill them."""
"1274","Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Darraj, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""What is between two leaves of a gate in Paradise is a journey of forty years."""
"1275","Zuhayr narrated to us, Rib'i ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah, from al-Harith, freedman of Ibn Siba', from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sings for riches, Allah will enrich him; and whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste."""
"1276","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, 'Isa narrated to us, from al-Mujalid, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Sa'id, who said: We had wine belonging to an orphan. When the verse in al-Ma'idah came down, we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it. We said: It belongs to an orphan. He said: ""Pour it out."""
"1277","And from Abu Sa'id, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The people of 'Illiyyun will be seen by those below them as you see the brilliant star on the horizon of the sky; and Abu Bakr and 'Umar are among them, and how excellent they are."""
"1278","Zuhayr narrated to us, Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, from Dhakwan, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The women said: Men have overcome us to you, O Messenger of Allah, so appoint for us a day. He said: He promised them a day; they came, and he admonished them. Among what he said to them was: ""There is no woman among you who sends forth three of her children but they will be for her a screen from the Fire?"" A woman said: O Messenger of Allah, and two? - two had died for her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""And two."""
"1279","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, who said: We were discussing Laylat al-Qadr, so we came to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri. I said to him: O Aba Sa'id, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention Laylat al-Qadr? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) observed i'tikaf in the middle ten of Ramadan, and we observed i'tikaf with him. When the morning of the twentieth came, he returned, and we returned with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept and saw Laylat al-Qadr in a dream, then he was made to forget it. He came out in the evening and addressed us. He said: ""I saw Laylat al-Qadr in a dream, then I was made to forget it; and I see myself that night prostrating in water and mud. Whoever observed i'tikaf with us, let him return to his place of i'tikaf. Seek it in the last ten, in the odd among them, for Allah is odd and loves the odd."" He said: We returned, and the sky rained upon us that evening; the roof of the mosque was a thatch of palm stalks. He observed i'tikaf. By the One who honoured him and sent down the Book upon him, I saw him on the night of the twenty-first, with his forehead and the tip of his nose in water and mud."
"1280","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, who said: We said to Abu Sa'id: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention the Haruriyyah? He said: I heard him say - and he mentioned the hadith."
"1281","Zuhayr narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sa'id, freedman of al-Mahri, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Banu Lihyan. He said: He said: ""Let one of every two men go forth, and the reward is between them."" Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, bless our sa' and our mudd, and join with the blessing two blessings."""
"1282","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abi Muslim, who said: I bear witness concerning Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id that they both bore witness concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""No people sit remembering Allah, mighty and majestic, but angels surround them, mercy covers them, tranquillity descends upon them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."""
"1283","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Abu Sa'id, freedman of al-Mahri, narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition to Banu Lihyan of Hudhayl. He said: Let one of every two men go forth, and the reward is between them. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'O Allah, bless for us our sa' and our mudd, and join with the blessing two blessings.'"""
"1284","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Amir narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Matar, from Ibn Sirin, from Dhakwan Abi Salih - and he praised him well - from Jabir and Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: ""They were forbidden sarf, and two men of them raised that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."""
"1285","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Amir narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will be rulers surrounded by hangers-on of people - or he said: courtiers. Shu'bah said: I think he said: They will wrong and lie. Whoever believes their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, nor am I of him; and whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their wrongdoing - he is of me and I am of him."""
"1286","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""When one of you comes upon a shepherd of camels, let him call: O shepherd of camels - three times. If he answers him, well; otherwise let him milk and drink, but let him not carry away. And when one of you comes upon a walled garden, let him call three times: O owner of the wall. If he answers him, well; otherwise let him eat but not carry away."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Hospitality is three days; what is more is charity."""
"1287","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Do not write from me anything other than the Qur'an; whoever wrote from me anything other than the Qur'an, let him erase it."""
"1288","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sleeps through witr or forgets it, let him pray witr when he remembers or wakes."""
"1289","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, who said: Ibn Shihab said: Abu Umamah ibn Sahl narrated to me that he heard Aba Sa'id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""While I was sleeping, I saw people presented with shirts upon them - some reaching the breasts, some reaching below that. And 'Umar ibn al-Khattab passed with a shirt he was dragging."" They said: How did you interpret that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""Religion."""
"1290","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Badr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'When there are three, let one of them lead them, and the most deserving of them for leading is the best reciter.'"""
"1291","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Sa'id, who said: We would estimate the standing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Zuhr and 'Asr. We estimated his standing in Zuhr in the first two rak'ahs as the measure of reciting thirty verses - like the measure of reciting Alif Lam Mim, Tanzil, al-Sajdah. In the last two rak'ahs, half of that. We estimated his standing in the first two rak'ahs of 'Asr as the measure of the last two of Zuhr, and the last two of 'Asr as half of that."
"1292","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, al-Mustamirr ibn al-Rayyan narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The world is green and sweet, so fear Allah and fear women."" He said: Then he mentioned three women who were among the Children of Israel: one short, and two tall. She made a leg of wood until she caught up with them, took a ring, made for it a lid, and filled it with the best of perfume: musk. When she passed a gathering, she opened the lid and the scent of musk spread."
"1293","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah Sa'id ibn Yazid, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will be a caliph who scoops wealth without counting it count."""
"1294","Zuhayr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Shayban - Yahya said: he informed me - from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, that Abu Salih informed him, that Abu Sa'id informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to a man of his Companions. He said: The man came out to him, headed to the watering place and bathed in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Did I hasten you?"" He said: O Messenger of Allah, I was between a woman's legs and did not emit. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then no washing is upon you."""
"1295","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, from al-Maqburi, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, who said: We were held back on the day of the Trench from Zuhr, 'Asr, Maghrib, and 'Isha', until we were relieved - and that is the saying of Allah: {And Allah sufficed the believers in fighting, and Allah is Strong, Mighty}. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, commanded Bilal, who called the iqamah. Then he prayed Zuhr as he used to pray it before that, then called the iqamah and prayed 'Asr as he used to pray it before that, then called the iqamah for Maghrib and prayed it as he used to pray it before that, then called the iqamah for 'Isha' and prayed it as he used to pray it before that - and that was before was revealed: {If you fear, then on foot or riding}."
"1296","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, al-Mustamirr ibn al-Rayyan narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Let not fear of a man - or fear of a human - prevent one of you from speaking the truth when he sees it or knows it."" Abu Sa'id said: I met Mu'awiyah and said to him: No maker of treachery but will have on the Day of Resurrection a banner of treachery for his treachery; and no treacherous one is greater than a ruler of the generality."
"1297","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Abd al-Ghafir, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man of those before you - Allah had given him wealth and children abundantly. When death came to him, he called his sons and said: What kind of father was I to you? They said: An excellent father. He said: By Allah, he never stored any good with Allah at all. When I die, burn me - until when I am charcoal, crush me, then scatter me on a windy day."" He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He took their pledges upon that, by my Lord; and they did, by my Lord: when he died, they burnt him; until when he was charcoal, they crushed him, then scattered him on a windy day. He said: His Lord said to him: Be - and behold, he was a standing man. His Lord said to him: What carried you to what you did? He said: My Lord, fear of Your punishment. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, He met him thereupon with forgiving him."" Qatadah said: A man feared the punishment of Allah, and Allah saved him through his fear."
"1298","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Salim, 'Abd Allah ibn Suhban, Kathir al-Nawwa', and Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The people of the highest ranks will be seen by those below them as you see the rising star on the horizon of the sky; and Abu Bakr and 'Umar are among them, and how excellent they are."""
"1299","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from al-Walid, from 'Abd Allah al-Bahi, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will be rulers over you to whom hearts feel secure and skins soften; then there will be rulers over you from whom skins shiver and hearts recoil."" He said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not fight them? He said: ""No, so long as they establish prayer."""
"1300","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Habib, freedman of Banu Zuhrah, from Abu al-Muthanna al-Juhani, who said: I was with Marwan ibn al-Hakam when Abu Sa'id al-Khudri came. Marwan said to him: Did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid blowing into drink? He said: ""Yes."""
"1301","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq informed us, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than a man who lost his mount in a desert land, sought it but could not find it, lay down for death - then while he is thus, he hears the jolt of his mount as it kneels; he uncovers his face, and behold, it is his mount."""
"1302","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, that Rafi', freedman of al-Shifa', informed him, who said: I and 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah entered upon Abu Sa'id al-Khudri visiting him. Abu Sa'id said to us: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us: Angels do not enter a house in which are statues or a picture."" Ishaq doubted; he does not know which of the two Abu Sa'id said."
"1303","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Khalid ibn Abi Nawf, from Salit, from Ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was performing ablution from the well of Buda'ah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you perform ablution from it when filth that is thrown into it is cast in it? He said: ""Water - nothing makes it impure."""
"1304","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'd al-Ta'i, from 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Companion of the Trumpet. He said: ""On his right is Jibril, and on his left is Mika'il."""
"1305","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from his brother Ma'bad ibn Sirin, who said: We said to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning 'azl? He said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about 'azl. He said: ""And what is 'azl?"" He said: We said: A man has a wife who is nursing; he has intercourse with her but dislikes her becoming pregnant, so he practices 'azl from her. And he has a slave-girl; he has intercourse with her but dislikes her becoming pregnant, so he practices 'azl from her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It does not matter if you do not do that, for it is only decree."""
"1306","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu al-'Alaniyah who said: We asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri about nabidh (fermented drink) prepared in the jarr (earthen jar), and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the jarr. He said: We said: What about the juff (wooden vessel)? He said: That is worse."
"1307","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Abu Sa'id who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying on a mat and prostrating on it."
"1308","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cool down (delay) the Zuhr prayer in extreme heat, for the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"1309","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id who said: I was walking with Ibn 'Umar in al-Balat, and he passed by a man dragging his izar (lower garment), and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drags his garments out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: I said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrating this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1310","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst of people in theft is the one who steals his prayer. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal it? He said: He does not complete its bowing nor its prostration."
"1311","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from 'Attab, from Abu Sa'id that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If Allah were to withhold rain from my ummah for ten years, then it was sent down, a group of my ummah would become disbelievers because of it, saying: It is due to the rising of al-Mijdah (a star)."
"1312","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib informed us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise and Hell boasted against each other. Hell said: O Lord, the tyrants, kings, great ones and nobles will enter me. And Paradise said: O Lord, the poor, weak and needy will enter me. So Allah said to Hell: You are My punishment, I afflict with you whomever I will. And He said to Paradise: You are My mercy, encompassing all things, and each one of you will have its fill. As for Hell, its people will be thrown into it, and it will say: Is there any more? Until the Blessed and Exalted comes to it and it is contracted, and it says: Enough, enough. And as for Paradise, there will remain in it what Allah wills to remain, then Allah will create for it a creation as He wills."
"1313","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Rashid, freedman of 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, who said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Most Merciful there is a Tablet containing three hundred and fifteen laws. The Most Merciful says: By My might and majesty, no servant of My servants who does not associate anything with Me comes with one of them, except that he will enter Paradise."
"1314","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Salim ibn Ghaylan informed us, that al-Walid ibn Qays al-Tujibi informed him, that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, or from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not accompany except a believer, and let none eat your food except a pious person."
"1315","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ibn Sayyad: What do you see? He said: I see a throne upon the sea with snakes around it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is the throne of Iblis."
"1316","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad informed us, al-'Ala - a man from Muzaynah - narrated to me, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that they were sitting reciting and supplicating. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them. He said: When we saw him we fell silent, and he said: Were you not doing such and such? He said: We said: Yes. He said: Then do as you were doing. And he sat with us, then he said: Give glad tidings to the poor Muhajirun of triumph on the Day of Resurrection over the rich by five hundred years, until the rich will wish that he had been poor, or destitute, in this world."
"1317","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abu 'Alqamah al-Hashimi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that on the day they conquered Awtas they captured women who had husbands, and some men among them disliked them (having relations with them), so Allah revealed this verse: And (forbidden are) married women except those whom your right hands possess."
"1318","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three gather, let one of them lead them, and the most entitled of them to lead is the most reciting (knowledgeable of the Qur'an) among them."
"1319","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu 'Isa al-Uswari, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Visit the sick, and follow funerals, they remind you of the Hereafter."
"1320","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked (prohibited) drinking while standing."
"1321","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Abu al-Waddak who said: I and a companion of mine differed about the hantam (green glazed jar), so we went to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and said to him: Narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the hantam? He said: If you say that, then at times during the era of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), some of us would attend and hear from him, and some of us would be occupied by their land, then he would come after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had stood up, and would say: What did he say? And we would inform him of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. And one day a drinker was brought, and he was pushed with hands and struck with sandals. He said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I did not drink wine. He said: Then what did you drink? He said: I took dates and raisins and put them in a gourd of mine. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing dates and raisins in the gourd and the muzaffat (pitched vessel)."
"1322","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Muslim al-'Abdi narrated to us, from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you drinks nabidh, let him drink it (made from) raisins alone, or dates alone, or unripe dates alone."
"1323","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) observed i'tikaf in the middle ten days of Ramadan seeking Laylat al-Qadr before it was made clear to him. When they ended, he ordered his structure to be dismantled, then it was made clear to him that it is in the last ten, so he ordered the structure to be restored and observed i'tikaf in the last ten. Then he came out to the people and said: O people, Laylat al-Qadr was made clear to me, then I came out to inform you of it, but I saw two men disputing with Satan among them, and I was made to forget it. So seek it on the ninth, seventh and fifth. I said: O Abu Sa'id, you know counting better than us. He said: We are more entitled to that than you. As for the ninth, seventh and fifth: he said: leave the one you call twenty-first, and the one after it is the ninth; and leave the one you call twenty-third, and the one after it is the seventh; and leave the one you call twenty-fifth, and the one after it is the fifth."
"1324","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm who said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri came to a man and said to him: Have you read what we have not read, and accompanied what we have not accompanied? He said: I have not read except what you have read, and you have accompanied. He said: Then why do you give fatwa to people (allowing) two dirhams for three, and a dirham for two dirhams? Then Abu Sa'id said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Gold for gold, like for like; whatever is extra is riba (usury). And silver for silver, like for like; whatever is extra is riba. He said: I heard him afterwards say: O Allah, I repent to You from what I used to give fatwa to people about in exchange."
"1325","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr who said: I and some men returning from 'umrah came, and we passed by Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and entered upon him. He said: Where do you intend? I said: We intend al-Tur (Mount Sinai). He said: And what is al-Tur? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The saddles of mounts are not tied (for worship) to a mosque in which Allah is remembered, except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the mosque of Madinah, and Bayt al-Maqdis. And prayer is not proper in two hours of the day: after Fajr until the sun rises, and after 'Asr until the sun sets. And fasting is not proper on two days of the year: the day of Fitr from Ramadan, and the day of Adha from Dhu al-Hijjah. And a woman should not travel on a journey in Islam except with a husband or a mahram."
"1326","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: Two men entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the price of a camel, so he helped them with two dinars. They left him and 'Umar met them, and they spoke well and thanked him for what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had done for them. So 'Umar entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what they said. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: But so-and-so, I gave him between ten and a hundred and he did not say that. One of them asks me and leaves carrying his request under his arm, and it is nothing but Fire. 'Umar said: Do you give us what is Fire? He said: They insist on asking me, and Allah refuses for me miserliness."
"1327","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim al-Azdi narrated to us, Sadaqah, the flour merchant, narrated to us, Malik ibn Dinar narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Ghalib al-Azdi, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Two traits do not combine in a believer: bad character and miserliness."
"1328","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, he said: I heard Darraj Abu al-Samh say: I heard Abu al-Haytham say: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: Ninety-nine dragons will be set upon the disbeliever in his grave, biting and stinging him until the Hour is established. If one of them were to breathe upon the earth, no green plant would grow."
"1329","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah informed us, Salim ibn Ghaylan informed me, that he heard Darraj Abu al-Samh, that he heard Abu al-Haytham, that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I seek refuge in Allah from disbelief and debt. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, do you equate debt with disbelief? He said: Yes."
"1330","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah is pleased with a servant, He praises him with nine kinds of good that he did not do, and when He is angry with a servant, He (allows) praise of him with nine kinds of evil that he did not do."
"1331","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to me, from Abu Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The example of the believer and the example of faith is like the example of a horse in its tether: it roams then returns to its tether. The believer slips, then returns to faith. So feed your food to the pious, and direct your kindness to the believers."
"1332","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban informed us, from Firas, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Charity is not lawful for a rich person, except if he has a poor neighbor who invites him and he eats with him, or the wayfarer, or (one striving) in the path of Allah."
"1333","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: This fire of yours is one part of seventy parts of the fire of Hell; each part of it has its heat."
"1334","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The righteous dream of the Muslim is one part of seventy parts of prophecy."
"1335","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The mujahid in the path of Allah is guaranteed by Allah: either He takes him to His forgiveness and mercy, or He returns him with reward and spoils. And the example of the mujahid in the path of Allah is like the one fasting and standing (in prayer), never flagging until he returns."
"1336","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Firas, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Avoid the supplications of the oppressed. And 'Atiyyah said: A man from the people of Khurasan said: Abu Hurayrah said: There is no veil between it and Allah."
"1337","And from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will be said to the companion of the Qur'an when he enters Paradise: Recite and ascend. So he will recite and ascend a degree with every verse, until he recites the last thing he has."
"1338","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid al-Wassafi narrated to us, from 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says when he goes to his bed: I seek forgiveness from Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer - three times - and I repent to Him, Allah will expiate his sins even if they are like the foam of the sea."
"1339","Zuhayr narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making nabidh in the hantam, dubba (gourd), and naqir (hollowed stump), and mixing unripe dates with ripe dates, and raisins with dates."
"1340","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sharfa, freedman of Ibn 'Umar, narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar narrated to me, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar who said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between my grave and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."
"1341","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, 'Isa ibn 'Abdullah ibn Malik narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Ata, from 'Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you intends a matter, let him say: O Allah, I seek Your choice by Your knowledge, and I seek ability by Your power, and I ask You of Your bounty, for You are able and I am not able, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if such-and-such - of the matter he intends - is good for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affair, and if not, then turn it away from me and turn me away from it, then decree for me good wherever it is. There is no power nor strength except in Allah."
"1342","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Maslamah ibn Qa'nab narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays al-Farra narrated to us, from 'Iyad ibn 'Abdullah, from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come out on the day of Eid - the day of Fitr - and pray with the people those two rak'ahs, then give salam and stand facing the people while they were sitting, and say: Give charity, give charity, three times. And the most who gave charity were the women, with earrings, rings and things. If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a need, or sent an expedition for the people, he mentioned it to them, otherwise he left."
"1343","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Maslamah ibn Qa'nab narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Nahhar al-'Abdi, that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri mention that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will question the servant on the Day of Resurrection until He says: What prevented you, when you saw evil, from denouncing it? Then when Allah inspires His servant with his proof, he says: My Lord, I trusted in You and feared the people."
"1344","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, 'Awf narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah will split into two groups, and a renegade group will emerge between them; the group closer to the truth will kill it."
"1345","Zuhayr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Ismah who said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the banner and shook it, then said: Who will take it with its due? Al-Zubayr came and said: I will. He said: Step aside. Then another man stood and said: I will. He said: Step aside. Then another stood and said: I will. He said: Step aside. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One who honored the face of Muhammad, I will give it to a man who will not flee with it. Here, O 'Ali. So he took it, then went until Allah opened Fadak and Khaybar, and he came with its 'ajwah (dates) and dried meat."
"1346","Zuhayr narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn 'Adi narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from 'Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to eat on the day of Fitr before going out, and he would not pray before the (Eid) prayer; when he returned, he prayed two rak'ahs."
"1347","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with truffles in his hand and said: These are of the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."
"1348","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr informed us, from 'Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent 'Alqamah ibn Mujazziz on an expedition in which I was. We set out until, when we were at the start of our raid or part of the way, a group sought his permission and he permitted them, appointing over them 'Abdullah ibn Hudhafah, who was among the people of Badr, and in whom there was jesting. I was among those who returned with him. While we were on part of the road, we stopped at a camp and the people kindled a fire to warm themselves or to prepare food on it, when 'Abdullah said to them: Do I not have hearing and obedience over you? They said: Yes. He said: Then whatever I command you, will you do it? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by my right and your obedience, except that you leap into this fire. He said: Some people stood and girded themselves, until when he thought they would leap into it, he said: Hold yourselves back; I was only joking with you. When they came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they mentioned that to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among them commands you to disobedience, do not obey him."
"1349","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri and Hammad ibn Salamah together informed us, from 'Amr ibn Yahya, from his father - Hammad said in his hadith: from Abu Sa'id - and Sufyan did not go beyond his father - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The whole earth is a mosque except the graveyard and the bathhouse."
"1350","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, 'Asim ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah al-Ansari, then al-Zafari, narrated to me, from Mahmud ibn Labid, one of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Gog and Magog will be opened upon the people, as Allah said: And they, from every elevation, descend. They will overwhelm the people, and the Muslims will withdraw from them to their cities and fortresses, gathering their livestock with them. They will drink the waters of the earth until some of them pass by a river and drink all that is in it until they leave it dry, so that those after them pass by that river and say: There was once water here. Until, when none of the people remain except some in a fortress or city, their speaker will say: These people of the earth, we are done with them; those of the heaven remain. He said: Then one of them will shake his spear, then throw it toward the sky, and it will return to him stained with blood, as trial and tribulation. While they are upon that, Allah will send worms in their necks like the naghaf of locusts that emerges in their necks, and they will die in the morning with no sound heard from them. The Muslims will say: Is there not a man who will sell himself for us to see what these enemies have done? He said: A man among them will strip himself for that, dedicating himself, having prepared it for being killed, and will find them dead, some upon others. He will call: O assembly of Muslims, rejoice, for Allah has sufficed you against your enemy. They will come out of their cities and fortresses and release their livestock, and they will have no pasture except their flesh, and they will grow fat as well as they ever grew fat from any vegetation they ever grazed."
"1351","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih. Ibn Shihab said: 'Ata ibn Yazid al-Junda'i informed me, that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri informed him, that some people from the Ansar asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no one asked him except that he gave him, until what he had was exhausted. When he had spent everything he had, he said: Whatever good I have, I will never withhold it from you. Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste; whoever seeks richness, Allah will enrich him; whoever strives to be patient, Allah will make him patient. And you have not been given a gift better nor more spacious than patience."
"1352","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding His saying: The day that some signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith - he said: The rising of the sun from its west."
"1353","Zuhayr narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad informed me, Dawud ibn Salih informed me, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: A Nabataean from Sham came with thirty loads of barley and dates during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he set a price - meaning a mudd for a dirham by the mudd of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and there was no food among the people that day other than it. The people complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the high price, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them and said: Shall I meet Allah, Blessed and Exalted, before I give anyone from anyone's wealth without his willing consent?"
"1354","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Shall I not guide you to something by which Allah expiates sins and increases good deeds? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Performing ablution thoroughly in disliked circumstances, many steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer. There is none among you who leaves his house purified, prays with the Muslims the congregational prayer, then sits in the mosque waiting for the next prayer, except that the angel says: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him. When you stand for prayer, straighten your rows, establish them, and close the gaps, for I see you from behind my back. When your imam says: Allah is Greatest, say: Allah is Greatest. When he bows, bow. When he says: Allah hears the one who praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise. The best of rows are the front, and the worst are the last; the best rows of women are the last, and the worst are the first. O assembly of women, when men prostrate, lower your gazes and do not see the private parts of men, due to the tightness of waist-wrappers."
"1355","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That a man killed ninety-nine souls, then asked about the most knowledgeable of the people of the earth and was directed to a man. He came to him and said: He killed ninety-nine souls; is there repentance for him? He said: After killing ninety-nine, there is no repentance for you. So he drew his sword and killed him, completing one hundred with him. He said: Then he remained as Allah willed, then asked about the most knowledgeable of the people of the earth, and was directed to a man. He said: He killed one hundred souls; is there repentance for him? He said: And who stands between you and repentance? Leave this evil village you are in for such-and-such village, and worship your Lord among them. He said: So he left, and his appointed time came upon him on the road. The angels of mercy and the angels of punishment disputed. Iblis said: He did not disobey me for a single hour ever. The angels of mercy said: He left repentant. Humayd al-Tawil claimed that Bakr narrated to him from Abu Rafi' who said: Allah sent an angel, and they gathered to him - the hadith returns to the hadith of Qatadah - he said: He said: Look to which of the two villages he was closer, and join him to its people. Qatadah said: So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brought the righteous village near, and distanced the evil one from him, and they joined him to its people."
"1356","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to me, from 'Amr ibn al-Harith, from Darraj, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truest dreams are at dawn (sahar)."
"1357","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi who said: Abu Sa'id said: A man from the Ansar said to his companions: By Allah, I used to tell you that if matters became settled for him, he would prefer others over you. He said: They answered him harshly. He said: That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he came to them and said things to them that I do not remember. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You used not to ride horses. He said: Whenever he said something to them, they said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. When he saw they were not answering him with anything, he said: Will you not say: Your people fought you and we helped you, and your people expelled you and we sheltered you? They said: We do not say that, O Messenger of Allah; you say it. He said: Then he said: O assembly of Ansar, are you not pleased that people go with this world and you go with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: O assembly of Ansar, are you not pleased that if people took a valley and you took a valley, I would take the valley of the Ansar? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar. The Ansar are my inner garment and household, my private trust to which I resort. Pardon their wrongdoers, and accept from their doers of good. Abu Sa'id said: Ibn Marjanah, the enemy of Allah, did not know that. Abu Sa'id said: I said to Mu'awiyah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not tell us that we would see after him favoritism (atharah)? Mu'awiyah said: Then what did he command you? He said: I said: He commanded us to be patient. He said: Then be patient."
"1358","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Madani narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to me, from Ibn 'Ajlan, from Nafi', from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three go out on a journey, let one of them lead them. Nafi' said: I said to Abu Salamah: You are our leader."
"1359","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Madani narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from 'Abdullah ibn Khabbab, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Abu Talib was mentioned in his presence - and he said: Perhaps my intercession will benefit him on the Day of Resurrection, so he will be placed in a shallow part of the Fire reaching his ankles, from which his brain will boil."
"1360","And from Abu Sa'id, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of the solitary by twenty-five degrees."
"1361","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The righteous dream is one part of forty-five parts of prophecy. Yazid said: I heard Abu Salamah narrating this hadith from Abu Hurayrah, to 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz. 'Umar said: If it were a pebble among pebbles, I would deem it true."
"1362","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he heard him say: When one of you sees a dream he loves, it is from Allah, so let him praise Allah for it and narrate it. And when he sees other than that of what he dislikes, it is from Satan, so let him seek refuge from its evil, and not mention it to anyone, for it will not harm him."
"1363","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the salam upon you, so how do we send salah upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, send salah upon Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, as You sent salah upon Ibrahim, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim."
"1364","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he would become junub (ritually impure) at night and want to sleep, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to perform ablution, then sleep."
"1365","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Sulayman al-A'mash narrated to us, from 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to narrate about the Dajjal. He said: He will be given power over a single soul; he will kill it then revive it, and say: Am I not your lord? And it will say: You were never more false in myself than you are now. He said: We used to think it was none but 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, until he died."
"1366","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibrahim Abu Ishaq al-Talqani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yazid Abu Shuja', from Abu al-Samh, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said (regarding): And they are frowning therein - he said: The Fire scorches him, so his lip contracts until it reaches the middle of his head, and the other relaxes until it strikes his navel."
"1367","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prefer some prophets over others."
"1368","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi' who said: A man narrated this hadith to Ibn 'Umar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrating it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he stood to him until he entered upon Abu Sa'id, and I was with him. He said: This one narrated to me from you a hadith you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); did you hear it? He said: My eye saw and my ear heard; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not sell gold for gold, nor silver for silver, except like for like. And do not sell something absent for something present."
"1369","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, Abu Salamah Sa'id ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for the people of the Fire who are its (permanent) people, they neither die therein nor live. But there are people - or as he said - whom sins befall - or he said: their errors - and it kills them a death, until when they become coal, permission is given for intercession, and they are brought in bundles upon bundles and scattered upon the rivers of Paradise. It will be said: O people of Paradise, pour upon them. So they will sprout as seeds sprout in the silt of a flood. A man among the people said then: It is as if the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had been in the desert."
"1370","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah who said: I asked Ibn 'Abbas about exchange (sarf). He said: Hand to hand. I said: Yes. He said: No harm. He said: Then I met Abu Sa'id and informed him that I had asked Ibn 'Abbas about exchange, and he said: No harm in it. He said: Did he say that? We shall write to him so he will not give you that fatwa. He said: By Allah, some youths of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with dates and he disapproved of them. He said: It seems this is not of the dates of our land? He said: There was something in last year's dates, so I took this and added some extra. He said: You have doubled, you have dealt in usury; do not approach this. When something of your dates troubles you, sell it, then buy the dates you want."
"1371","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id who said: We used to go out to battle with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Ramadan; among us were fasting and among us were breaking fast. The fasting did not find fault with the breaking, nor the breaking with the fasting. They deemed that whoever found strength and fasted, that is good; and they deemed that whoever found weakness and broke fast, that is good."
"1372","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying wrapped (in a single garment)."
"1373","Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lah'ah narrated to us, Darraj Abu al-Samh narrated to us, that Abu al-Haytham narrated to him, from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, glad tidings to whoever saw you and believed in you. He said: Glad tidings to whoever saw me and believed in me, then glad tidings, then glad tidings, then glad tidings to whoever believed in me and did not see me. A man said to him: And what is Tuba? He said: A tree in Paradise, a hundred years' journey; the garments of the people of Paradise come out of its sheaths."
"1374","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A man said: What is like molten brass? He said: Like the sediment of oil; when he brings it near him, the skin of his face falls off from it."
"1375","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Remember Allah with much remembrance until they say: Mad."
"1376","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If a mountain were struck with an iron hammer, it would crumble, then return as it was."
"1377","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: If one of you were to work inside a solid rock that has no door nor window, his deed would emerge to the people, whatever it is."
"1378","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Every letter in the Qur'an in which qunut is mentioned means obedience."
"1379","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Jibril came to me and said: Your Lord and my Lord says: How have I raised your remembrance? He said: And Allah knows best. He said: When I am mentioned, you are mentioned with Me."
"1380","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If a bucket of ghassaq (festering pus) were poured into this world, the people of this world would stink."
"1381","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Dust will consume everything of man except his tailbone. It was said: And what is it like, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Like a mustard seed; from it they will sprout."
"1382","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Wayl is a valley in Hell into which the disbeliever falls for forty autumns (years) before reaching its bottom. And he said: Al-Sa'ud is a mountain of fire up which he climbs for seventy autumns, then falls down likewise in it forever."
"1383","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Increase in the enduring righteous deeds. It was said: And what are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The (true) religion. It was said: And what is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Tahlil (La ilaha illa Allah), takbir (Allahu Akbar), tasbih (Subhan Allah), praise of Allah (Alhamdulillah), and there is no power nor strength except in Allah."
"1384","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There will be erected for the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection (a period) of fifty thousand years, as he did not work for Allah in this world. And the disbeliever will see Hell and think it will befall him from a distance of forty years."
"1385","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man will recline in Paradise for seventy years before moving. Then a woman will come to him and strike his shoulders; he will look at his face in her cheek, clearer than a mirror. The least pearl upon her will light up what is between the east and the west. She will greet them, and he will return her salam and ask her: Who are you? She will say: I am she of the increase (al-mazid). Upon her will be seventy garments, the least of them like al-Nu'man from Tuba. His sight will pierce them until he sees the marrow of her shin from behind that. Upon them are crowns; the least pearl in them lights up what is between the east and the west."
"1386","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Winter is the spring of the believer."
"1387","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The seat of the disbeliever in the Fire is three days (journey); each molar of his like Uhud, his thigh like Warqan, and his skin apart from his flesh and bones, forty cubits."
"1388","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If an iron hammer were placed on the earth and the two heavy (creations, men and jinn) gathered upon it, they could not lift it from the earth."
"1389","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The enclosure wall of the Fire has four walls; between each wall is like forty years."
"1390","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, a day whose measure is fifty thousand years - how long is this! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, it will be lightened upon the believer until it is lighter upon him than a prescribed prayer he prays in this world."
"1391","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will remember Allah in this world upon spread beds; He will admit them to the highest gardens."
"1392","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, the disbeliever will be informed of his deed, and he will deny and dispute. It will be said: These are your neighbors testifying against you. He will say: They lied. He will say: Your family, your tribe? He will say: They lied. He will say: Swear. So they will swear. Then Allah will silence them and their tongues will testify, then He will admit them to the Fire."
"1393","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Musa said: O Lord, teach me something by which I remember You and call upon You. He said: Say, O Musa: There is no god but Allah. He said: All Your servants say this. He said: Say: There is no god but Allah. He said: There is no god but You; I want something You single me out with. He said: O Musa, if the seven heavens and their inhabitants other than Me, and the seven earths, were in a scale, and There is no god but Allah were in a scale, There is no god but Allah would outweigh them."
"1394","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Gatherings are three: safe, gaining, and perishing."
"1395","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said (regarding): And raised couches - he said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, its height is as between heaven and earth, and what is between heaven and earth is a journey of five hundred years."
"1396","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Boasting (about intercourse) is forbidden. Ibn Lah'ah said: Meaning one who boasts of intercourse."
"1397","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps a man earns wealth from lawful means and feeds himself, and a man has wealth in which there is charity, and he says: O Allah, send salah upon Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, and send salah upon the believing men and believing women and Muslim men and Muslim women; for it is zakah (purification) for him."
"1398","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise has one hundred degrees; if all the worlds gathered in one of them, it would contain them."
"1399","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan said: By Your might, O Lord, I will not cease misleading Your servants as long as their souls are in their bodies. The Lord said: By My might and majesty, I will not cease forgiving them as long as they seek My forgiveness."
"1400","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, even two sheep will dispute over what they butted each other for."
"1401","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which worship is highest in degree with Allah on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Those who remember Allah much. I said: O Messenger of Allah, and the one who strives in the path of Allah? He said: If he struck the disbelievers and polytheists with his sword until it broke and became dyed with blood, the one who remembers Allah would be better than him."
"1402","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: A man migrated to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Yemen, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You have abandoned shirk, but it is jihad. Are your parents in Yemen? He said: Yes. He said: Did they permit you? He said: No. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return to your parents and seek their permission; if they allow, then strive, otherwise be dutiful to them."
"1403","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Lord says on the Day of Resurrection: The people of the gathering will know today who are the people of nobility. It was said: And who are the people of nobility? He said: The people of remembrance in the mosques."
"1404","And from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in rank is one who has eighty thousand servants and seventy-two wives. A dome of pearl, ruby and peridot will be erected for him, as between al-Jabiyah and San'a."
"1405","And from Abu Sa'id, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Abu Khaythamah doubted - from Abu Sa'id, that he said: Whoever of the people of this world dies, young or old, they are returned to sixty years in Paradise; they never exceed it. And likewise the people of the Fire."
"1406","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Qatadah, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Abd al-Ghafir, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will take his father's hand on the Day of Resurrection to cut through the Fire with him, wanting to admit him to Paradise, then it will be called out that Paradise is not entered by a polytheist. Indeed Allah has forbidden Paradise to every polytheist. He will say: My Lord, my father, my father, my father. He said: Then he will be transformed into an ugly form and foul smell, and he will be abandoned. Abu Sa'id said: The companions of Muhammad deemed that man to be Ibrahim, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not add to them beyond that."
"1407","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Bishr ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He forbade continuous fasting (wisal). It was said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you do it? He said: I am not like any of you; I am fed and given drink."
"1408","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Humayd, from Abu Malih who said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you performs prayer, then returns to his house, let him pray, and let him give his house a share of his prayer, for Allah will place good in his house from his prayer."
"1409","I recited to al-Husayn ibn Yazid al-Tahhan: Sa'id ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Fudayl, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: When this verse was revealed: And give the relative his right - the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Fatimah and gave her Fadak."
"1410","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Qays ibn Wahb, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will emerge, and a man from the Muslims will head toward him. The armed guards - the guards of the Dajjal - will meet him and say to him: Where do you intend? He will say: I intend this one who has emerged. They will say to him: Do you not believe in our lord? He said: He will say: I do not see - I think - (it as) true. He said: They will say: Kill him. He said: Some of them will say to others: Did your lord not forbid you to kill anyone without him? He said: So they will take him to the Dajjal. He said: When the believer sees him, he will say: O people, this is the Dajjal whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned. He said: So the Dajjal will order him to be stretched out. He said: He will say: Take him and stretch him out. He said: So he will be stretched. He said: His back and stomach will be beaten severely. He said: He will say to him: Do you not believe in me? He said: He will say: You are the false Messiah. He said: So he will order him to be sawn with a saw from his parting until he is split between his legs. He said: Then the Dajjal will walk between the two pieces. He said: Then he will say: Stand, and he will stand upright. He said: He will say to him: Do you not believe in me? He said: He will say to him: I have only increased in insight about you. He said: Then he will say: O people, he will not do to anyone among the people what he did to me. He said: The Dajjal will take him to slaughter him, but what is between his chin and his collarbone will be made copper, so he cannot get at him. He said: So he will take his hands and legs and throw him. People will think he threw him into the Fire, but he was only cast into Paradise. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the greatest of people in testimony with the Lord of the worlds."
"1411","Qatan ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: When Yazid ibn al-Muhallab defeated the people of Basra, al-Mu'alla said: I feared sitting in the circle of al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, lest I be noticed therein and recognized. So I went to al-Hasan in his house and entered upon him. I said: O Abu Sa'id, what about this verse from the Book of Allah? He said: Which verse from the Book of Allah? I said: The saying of Allah in this verse: And you see many of them hastening into sin and aggression and their consuming of unlawful gain; evil is what they were doing. He said: O servant of Allah, the people brandished the sword, and the sword stood between speech. I said: O Abu Sa'id, do you know any merit for one who speaks? He said: No. Al-Mu'alla said: Then he narrated two hadiths. He said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to us, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a hadith. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the fear of people not prevent one of you from speaking the truth when he sees it, mentioning the greatness of Allah; for it neither brings an appointed time near, nor distances provision. He said: Then al-Hasan narrated another hadith: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not for the believer to humiliate himself. It was said: And what is humiliating himself? He said: He exposes himself to trial he cannot bear. It was said: O Abu Sa'id, what about Yazid al-Dabbi and his speech in prayer? He said: He did not leave prison until he regretted. Al-Mu'alla said: So I rose from al-Hasan's gathering and went to Yazid. I said: O Abu Mawdud, while I and al-Hasan were conversing, I raised your matter pointedly. He said: Hush, O Abu al-Hasan. He said: I said: I did. He said: Then what did al-Hasan say? I said: He said: He did not leave prison until he regretted his statement. Yazid said: I did not regret my statement; by Allah, I stood in a stand in which I risked my life. Yazid said: So I went to al-Hasan and said: O Abu Sa'id, we have been overcome in everything; shall we be overcome in our prayer? He said: O servant of Allah, you have done nothing; you expose yourself to them. Then I went to him, and he said to me the like of his statement. He said: So I stood on Friday in the mosque while al-Hakam ibn Ayyub was addressing. I said: May Allah have mercy on you, the prayer. He said: When I said that, men surrounded me, attacking me. They took my beard and collar, and struck my belly with the scabbards of their swords. He said: They took me toward the maqsurah (enclosure), and I did not reach it until I thought they would kill me short of him. He said: The door of the maqsurah was opened for me. He said: I entered and stood before al-Hakam while he was silent. He said: Are you mad? He said: And we were not in prayer. I said: May Allah set right the amir, is there any speech better than the Book of Allah? He said: No. I said: May Allah set right the amir, what if a man spread a mushaf reciting it morning to night, would that suffice him for his prayer? He said: By Allah, I think you are mad. He said: And Anas ibn Malik was sitting beneath his pulpit, silent. I said: O Anas, O Abu Hamzah, I adjure you by Allah, for you served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and accompanied him: did I say what is right or wrong? Did I say truth or falsehood? He said: By Allah, he did not answer me a word. Al-Hakam ibn Ayyub said to him: O Anas. He said: He said: At your service, may Allah set you right. He said: The time of prayer had passed; there remained of the sun a remnant. He said: Detain him. Yazid said: I swear to you, O Abu al-Hasan - meaning al-Mu'alla - what I met from my companions was harder upon me than my stand. Some said: A show-off. And some said: Mad. He said: Al-Hakam wrote to al-Hajjaj: A man from Banu Dabbah stood on Friday saying: The prayer, while I was addressing, and upright witnesses testified to me that he is mad. Al-Hajjaj wrote to him: If upright witnesses have testified that he is mad, let him go; otherwise cut off his hands and feet, brand his eyes, and crucify him. He said: They testified before al-Hakam that I am mad, so he released me. Al-Mu'alla said: From Yazid al-Dabbi: A brother of ours died, so we followed his funeral and prayed over him. When he was buried, I withdrew with a group, and we remembered Allah and remembered our return. While we were thus, we saw the forelocks of horses and spears. When my companions saw them, they stood and left me alone. Al-Hakam came until he stood over me and said: What were you doing? I said: May Allah set right the amir, a companion of ours died, so we prayed over him and he was buried. We sat remembering our Lord, remembering our return, and remembering what he has become. He said: What prevented you from fleeing as they fled? I said: May Allah set right the amir, I am innocent of that and safer for the amir than to flee. He said: Al-Hakam fell silent. 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Muhallab - who was over his police - said: Do you know who this is? He said: Who is this? He said: The one who spoke on Friday. He said: Al-Hakam became angry and said: You are insolent; seize him. He said: So I was seized and he struck me four hundred lashes. I did not know, when he left me, from the severity of his beating. He said: He sent me to Wasit, and I was in al-Hajjaj's prison until al-Hajjaj died. Up to here is the musnad of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri."
"1412","Musnad of Rukanah: Abu Ya'la informed us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, he said: I met in Makkah a man from the people of 'Asqalan called Abu al-Hasan, and he narrated to me, from Abu Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Rukanah, from his father, that he wrestled the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Rukanah said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The difference between us and the polytheists is turbans over caps."
"1413","Musnad of Buraydah: Abu Ya'la informed us, he said: It was recited to Bishr ibn al-Walid, from Abu Yusuf, from Abu Hanifah, from 'Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That when he sent an expedition or army, he enjoined its leader to fear Allah in himself specially, and enjoined him to be good to those Muslims with him. Then he said: Fight in the name of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not steal spoils, do not betray, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child. When you meet your enemy among the polytheists, call them to Islam. If they accept Islam, accept from them and refrain from them. Then call them to move from their abode to the abode of the Muslims. If they do, accept from them; otherwise inform them that they are like the Bedouin Muslims: the ruling of Allah that applies to Muslims applies to them, and they have no share in the fay nor in the spoils. If they refuse that, call them to pay the jizyah. If they do, accept from them and refrain from them. When you besiege a fortress or city, if they want you to let them down upon the judgment of Allah, do not let them down; for you do not know what the judgment of Allah is. But let them down upon your judgment, then judge concerning them as you see fit. And when you besiege a palace, do not give them the covenant of Allah nor the covenant of His Messenger, but give them your covenants and your fathers' covenants; for your breaking your covenants and your fathers' covenants is lighter."
"1414","Musnad of Abu Talhah, may Allah be pleased with him: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Abu Talhah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."
"1415","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh and 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, both said: Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Talhah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he overcame a people, liked to stay in their courtyard three (days)."
"1416","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar and Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Abu Talhah informed me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and 'Umrah."
"1417","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Ishaq ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Abu Talhah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned rams; at the first slaughter he said: On behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and at the second slaughter he said: On behalf of whoever of my ummah believed in me and affirmed me."
"1418","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Ishaq ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Abu Talhah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned rams; at the first slaughter he said: On behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and at the other slaughter he said: On behalf of whoever of my ummah believed in me and affirmed me."
"1419","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Abu Talhah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined Hajj and 'Umrah."
"1420","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, from Abu Talhah: That he entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the illness in which he died, and he said: Convey salam to your people, for they, as far as I know, are chaste and patient."
"1421","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, Ishaq ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, he said: Abu Talhah said: We were sitting in the courtyards talking, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and stood over us. He said: What is with you and the gatherings of the roads? Avoid the gatherings of the roads. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, we sat for no harm: we sat remembering and talking. He said: If not, then give its due. We said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is its due? He said: Lowering the gaze, returning the salam, and good speech."
"1422","'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath Abu Bahr narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: Abu Talhah said: I raised my head on the day of Uhud and looked; there was none among them except that he was swaying from drowsiness beneath his shield."
"1423","Abu Bahr narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from al-Zubayr the like of it, and he recited: Then He sent down upon you after distress, security, drowsiness covering a group."
"1424","Al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Jurjani narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The sky rained hail, and Abu Talhah said to us, while we were youths: Hand me, O Anas, some of that hail. He began eating while fasting. I said: Are you not fasting? He said: Yes; this is neither food nor drink; it is only a blessing from heaven by which we purify our stomachs. Anas said: So I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Take from your uncle."
"1425","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn 'Amr al-Jazari narrated to us, Zayd ibn Rufay' narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from Abu Talhah, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while his face was radiant, rejoicing. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you are in a state I never saw you in the like of. He said: And what prevents me? Jibril came to me and said: Give your ummah glad tidings: whoever sends salah upon you once, Allah writes for him ten good deeds, expiates from him ten evil deeds, raises for him ten degrees, Allah returns to him the like of his saying, and it will be presented to him on the Day of Resurrection."
"1426","Muhammad ibn 'Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah - meaning Ibn Abi Muzarrid - from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah al-Ansari, from his father 'Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Abu Talhah, who said: I entered the mosque and recognized hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I went out until I came to Umm Sulaym - she is the mother of Anas ibn Malik, who was under Malik, the father of Anas ibn Malik - and I said: O Umm Sulaym, I have recognized hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); is there anything with you? She said: There is something with me, and she gestured with her palm. I said: Prepare and do well. So I sent Anas to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I said: Whisper in his ear and invite him. When Anas approached, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is a man who has come with good. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did your father send you to invite us, O my son? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Go, in the name of Allah. He said: Anas turned running until he came to Abu Talhah and said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) coming to you with the people. He said: So I went out until I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the door at the resting of the stairs. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what have you done to us? I only recognized hunger in your face, and we prepared for you something to eat. He said: Enter and rejoice. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and gathered it in the dish with his hand, then fixed it. He said: Is there any? As if meaning condiment. He said: They brought him their skin vessel in which was something, or in which was nothing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did with it with his hand, and ghee poured from it. Then he said: Admit ten by ten. They all ate and were satisfied. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of the leftover that remained: Eat, you and your family. So they ate and were satisfied."
"1427","Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Zajir ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn 'Umayr, from Shaddad, from Abu Talhah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O youths of Quraysh, do not commit adultery; whoever has his youth preserved for him, Paradise is his."
"1428","Abu Mu'mar al-Hudhali narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, from Abu Talhah who said: The sword fell from me on the day of Badr due to the drowsiness that overcame us. Allah says: When He covered you with drowsiness as security from Him."
"1429","'Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh al-'Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, from Abu Talhah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Perform ablution from what fire has altered (cooked)."
"1430","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Abu Talhah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."
"1431","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ar'arah narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: Anas mentioned to us, from Abu Talhah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered on the day of Badr concerning twenty-four men of the chiefs of Quraysh, and they were cast into a foul, defiled well among the wells of Badr. When he prevailed over a people, he liked to stay in their courtyard three nights. When at Badr on the third day, he ordered his mount and its saddle was fastened upon it. Then he walked and his companions followed him. They said: We do not think he goes except to relieve himself. Until he stood at the edge of the well, and began calling them by their names and their fathers' names: O so-and-so son of so-and-so, O so-and-so son of so-and-so, would it please you that you had obeyed Allah and His Messenger? We have found what our Lord promised us true; have you found what your Lord promised true? He said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you speak to bodies that have no souls? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, you are not more hearing of what I say than they are. Qatadah said: Allah gave them life until He made them hear as rebuke, belittling, vengeance, grief and regret."
"1432","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Talhah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Angels do not enter a house in which there are images or a dog. Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani said to Abu Talhah: Take us to 'A'ishah to ask her about this. So they went to 'A'ishah and asked her. She said: As for this, I do not remember it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). But the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on one of his expeditions, and I awaited his return and covered the dais of the house with a patterned cloth. When he entered, I greeted him and took his hand. I said: Praise be to Allah who aided you, honored you and ennobled you. He looked at it and I saw dislike in his face. And he mentioned the hadith in full."
"1433","Musnad of Qays ibn Sa'd: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Qays ibn Sa'd - as a report - who said: If faith were suspended from the Pleiades, men from the people of Persia would attain it."
"1434","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abu 'Ammar, from Qays ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to give Zakat al-Fitr before zakah was revealed. When zakah was revealed, he neither commanded us nor forbade us, and we do it."
"1435","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn As'ad ibn Zurarah, from Muhammad ibn Shurahbil, from Qays ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, so we placed water for him and he bathed. Then we brought him a dyed wrap with wars (yellow dye) and he wrapped himself in it, and it is as if I look at the trace of the wars upon his sides."
"1436","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Ibn Hubayrah narrated to me, he said: I heard an elder narrating to Abu Tamim, that he heard Qays ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, while he was over Egypt, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take a house in Hell, or a resting place in Hell. And whoever drinks wine will come on the Day of Resurrection thirsty. Every intoxicant is wine, and beware of al-ghubayra. And I heard 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr say the like of that; they differed only in resting place or house."
"1437","Abu Ya'la said: I found in my book: From 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd, from Shu'bah, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibn Abi Layla, who said: Sahl ibn Hunayf and Qays ibn Sa'd were sitting at al-Qadisiyyah, and a funeral passed by them, so they stood. It was said to them: He is only of the people of the land. They said: A funeral passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he stood. It was said: It is the funeral of a disbeliever. He said: Is it not a soul? Abu Ya'la said: I found in my book: From 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd, from Shu'bah, and there is no mark of hearing upon it, so I doubted it."
"1438","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Qays ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If faith were suspended from the Pleiades, men from the sons of Persia would attain it."
"1439","Musnad of Abu Rayhanah: Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, Humayd al-Kindi narrated to us, from 'Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abu Rayhanah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever claims descent from nine disbelieving forefathers, seeking by them nobility and honor, he is their tenth in the Fire."
"1440","Musnad of 'Uthman ibn Hunayf: Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, who said: I went out with 'Uthman ibn Hunayf visiting Abu Talhah in an illness of his. He said: We entered upon him, and beneath him was a figured cloth upon his bed, in which was an image of statues. He said: Remove this from beneath me. 'Uthman said to him: Did you not hear, O Abu Talhah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say when he forbade images: Except a figure in a garment, or a garment in which is a figure? He said: Yes, but it is better for myself that it not be placed beneath me."
"1441","Musnad of Abu Waqid al-Laythi: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to Khaybar, passed by a tree upon which the polytheists hung their weapons, called Dhat Anwant. They said: O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anwant. He said: Allah is Greatest; this is as the people of Musa said to Musa: Make for us a god as they have gods. You will ride the practice of those before you."
"1442","Abu Bakr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman, from Nafi' ibn Sarjis Abu Sa'id, that he heard Abu Waqid al-Laythi, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and prayer was mentioned in his presence - and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer over the people, and the most enduring upon himself."
"1443","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Damrah ibn Sa'id, who said: I heard 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah say: 'Umar went out on a day of Eid and asked Abu Waqid al-Laythi: With what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite on this day? He said: With Qaf and Iqtarabat (the Moon has split)."
"1444","'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban al-Kufi, nephew of Husayn al-Ju'fi, narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from a son of Abu Waqid al-Laythi, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from his father, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to his wives in the year of the Farewell Hajj: This, then (remaining upon) the backs of mats (stay at home)."
"1445","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Ishaq ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to me, from Hurayth Abu Murrah, that Abu Waqid al-Laythi narrated to him, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), three men passed. One of them came and found a gap in the circle and sat; another sat behind them; the third went away. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you about these men? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: As for the one who came and sat, he sought shelter, so Allah sheltered him. As for the one who sat behind you, he was shy, so Allah was shy of him. As for the one who went away, he is a man who turned away, so Allah turned away from him."
"1446","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Damrah ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, who heard 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah say: 'Umar went out on a day of Eid and asked Abu Waqid al-Laythi: With what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite on this day? He said: With Qaf, and Iqtarabat."
"1447","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, from Fulayh, from Damrah ibn Sa'id, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: 'Umar asked me: With what did the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in the two Eids? I said: With Iqtarabati al-Sa'ah wa Inshaqqa al-Qamar, and Qaf wa al-Qur'an al-Majid."
"1448","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn Sarjis, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, that he heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer and the most enduring upon himself."
"1449","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Warraq narrated to us, Husayn al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Ibn Khuthaym al-Makki, from Nafi' ibn Sarjis, who said: I entered upon Abu Waqid al-Laythi in Makkah during the illness in which he died, and I heard him say, or he said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer and the most enduring upon himself."
"1450","'Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah ibn Dinar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah while people were cutting off camels' humps and cutting sheep tails. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever is cut from the animal while it is alive is dead (carrion)."
"1451","Musnad of Abd Allah al-Sunabihi (1): Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah al-Sunabihi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun rises along with the horn of Satan; when it has risen high it leaves it; when it reaches midday it joins it; when it declines it leaves it; when it nears sunset it joins it; when it has set it leaves it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer during those hours."
"1452","(2): Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Mujalid ibn Sa'id, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Sunabihi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will boast of your numbers before the nations, so do not turn back after me as disbelievers, some of you striking the necks of others."
"1453","(3): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Sunabihi al-Ahmasi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a fine she-camel among the camels of charity and said: May Allah destroy the owner of this she-camel. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I took it back in exchange for two camels from the inferior camels. He said: Then yes, that is fine."
"1454","(4): Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak and Waki' narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from al-Sunabihi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I am going ahead of you at the Hawd (Pool), and I will boast of your numbers before the nations, so do not fight one another after me."
"1455","(5): Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Numayr and Abu Usama narrated to us, they said: Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays, from al-Sunabihi al-Ahmasi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"1456","Musnad of Amr ibn Hurayth (1): Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Hurayth saying: My mother took me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he wiped my head and supplicated for me for provision."
"1457","(2): Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifa narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Sari', the mawla of the family of Amr ibn Hurayth, from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: I prayed Fajr behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I heard him reciting: So I swear by the retreating stars, those that run and hide. He said: And none of us would bend his back until he (the Prophet) stood straight after prostrating."
"1458","(3): Ubayd Allah ibn Umar ibn Maysara al-Jushami narrated to us, Afif ibn Salim al-Mawsili narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: I sold a house and land of mine in Madina, and my brother Sa'id ibn Hurayth said to me: Keep away from it as much as you can and do not spend any of it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever sells a house or real estate, he is likely not to be blessed in it unless he puts it into something like it. Amr said: So I bought with part of its price this house of mine, meaning the house of Amr ibn Hurayth."
"1459","(4): Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Musawir al-Warraq, from Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Hurayth, from his father, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a black turban."
"1460","(5): al-Qawariri narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Musawir al-Warraq, from Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Hurayth, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us wearing a black turban."
"1461","(6): Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Sari', from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in Fajr: And the night as it departs."
"1462","(7): Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes touch his beard during prayer."
"1463","(8): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Asbagh, from Amr ibn Hurayth - and Mu'tamir, a mawla of Amr ibn Hurayth, said, from Amr ibn Hurayth - he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he recited, and it is as if I hear his voice saying: So I swear by the retreating stars, those that run and hide. Muhammad ibn Yazid said in his hadith: And my mother or my father took me to him, and he supplicated for me for provision."
"1464","(9): al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Fitr ibn Khalifa, from his father, from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marked out for me a house in Madina with a bow, and said: Shall I give you more."
"1465","(10): al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Suddi, one who heard Amr ibn Hurayth narrated to me, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in two patched sandals."
"1466","(11): Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from one who heard Amr ibn Hurayth, saying: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in two patched sandals."
"1467","(12): Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Fitr, from his father, from Amr ibn Hurayth, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Abd Allah ibn Ja'far while he was selling with the slave-boys or children, and said: O Allah, bless him in his sale - or he said: in his bargain."
"1468","(13): Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mis'ar, al-Walid ibn Sari' narrated to me, from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in the morning prayer: And the night as it departs - or he said: When the sun is folded up."
"1469","(14): Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from a mawla of Amr ibn Hurayth, from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: I prayed Fajr with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he recited: When the sun is folded up; it is as if I hear his voice saying: So I swear by the retreating stars, those that run and hide. And he said: My mother and my father took me to him, and he supplicated for me for provision."
"1470","(15): Abu Sa'id al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truffle is from the manna, and its water is a cure for the eye."
"1471","(16): Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Ali, from Muhammad ibn Suqa, from his father, he said: I came to Amr ibn Hurayth to rent a house from him in his residence, and he said: Rent it, for it is blessed for its owner, blessed for whoever lives in it. I said: How is that? He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a camel had been slaughtered and he had ordered its distribution, and he said to the one distributing it: Give Amr a share of it, but he did not give me and overlooked me. The next day I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while there were dirhams in front of him, and he said: Did you receive the share I ordered for you? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, he gave me nothing. He said: So he took a handful of dirhams and gave them to me, and I brought them to my mother and said: Take these dirhams; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took them with his hand and gave them to me; keep them until we see what to put them into. Then time passed until I bought this house. My mother said: When you want to pay its price, do not pay until you call me to supplicate for blessing for you. So I called her when I had arranged it, and she said to me: Take these dirhams; I scattered them in it, then mixed them with it, and she said: Go with them."
"1472","Musnad of Amr ibn Hurayth (another man mentioned by Abu Khaythama) (1): Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, and Ahmad ibn al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to me, Abu Hani' narrated to me, Amr ibn Hurayth narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever you lighten of your servant's work, its reward is in your scales."
"1473","(2): Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywa narrated to us, he said: Abu Hani' Humayd ibn Hani' al-Khawlani informed me, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, who is Abd Allah ibn Yazid, and Amr ibn Hurayth, and others, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will come to a people whose heads are curly; treat them well, for they are a strength for you and a provision against your enemy by Allah's permission - meaning the Copts of Egypt."
"1474","Musnad of Haritha ibn Wahb (1): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash and Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Wahb, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina - when the people were safest and most numerous - two rak'as."
"1475","(2): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, he said: I heard Haritha ibn Wahb al-Khuza'i, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity, for soon a man will go out with his charity and find no one to accept it."
"1476","(3): Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Haritha ibn Wahb, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jawwaz will not enter Paradise, nor the Ja'zari. He said: And the Jawwaz is the coarse, harsh person."
"1477","(4): Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Hajjaj - or another - narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, Ma'bad ibn Khalid narrated to us, that he heard Haritha ibn Wahb al-Khuza'i, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise? Every weak, oppressed person, who if he swore by Allah, Allah would fulfill it; and the people of Hell are every arrogant Jawwaz."
"1478","(5): Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Dawud, from Abbas, from Kindir ibn Sa'id, from his father, he said: I performed Hajj in the days of ignorance, and there was a man circumambulating the House reciting poetry. I said: Who is this, meaning? They said: Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim; some camels of his were lost, so he sent his son's son to seek them, but he was delayed, though he never sent him for a need but he accomplished it. He said: I did not leave until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and brought the camels, and he said: O my son, I grieved for you this time with a grief that will never leave me."
"1479","(6): Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Aws al-Absi narrated to us, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from his father Shakl ibn Humayd, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a refuge to seek. He took my hand and said: Say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul, and from the evil of my hearing, and from the evil of my sight, and from the evil of my heart, and from the evil of my tongue, and from the evil of my semen."
"1480","(7): Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, he said: I was sitting with Yazid ibn Abi Muslim in the days of al-Hajjaj while he was torturing people, and he mentioned a man in prison, so he sent for him in anger and rage, and he was brought. When he stood before him, I saw the man move his lips with something I did not hear, so he raised his head to him and said: Let him go - or he said: Send him back. He said: So I went to the man and said: I witnessed this when he sent for you in anger and rage, and I had no doubt he would harm you; when you stood before him I saw you move your lips with something I did not hear, then he ordered concerning you what you see, so what did you say? He said: I said: O Allah, I ask You by Your power by which You hold the seven heavens lest some of them fall upon others, to suffice me against him."
"1481","(8): al-Tarjumani Abu Ibrahim narrated to us, Ubays ibn Maymun narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is none of you able to recite in the night: Say, He is Allah, One? For it equals the whole Qur'an. He said: And he said: People must have a chief, and the chief is in Hell. He said: And the policeman will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to him: Put down your whip and enter Hell."
"1482","(9): Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi al-Hakam al-Ghifari saying: My grandmother narrated to me, from the uncle of Abu Rafi' ibn Amr al-Ghifari, he said: When I was a boy I used to throw stones at the date-palms of the Ansar, and it was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Here is a boy throwing stones at our date-palms - or he said: throwing at the palms. He said: So I was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O boy, do not throw at the palms. He said: I said: To eat. He said: Do not throw at the palms; eat what falls. He said: And he wiped his head and said: O Allah, fill his belly."
"1483","Musnad of Mu'adh ibn Anas (1): Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Asid ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Farwa ibn Mujahid, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh al-Juhani, he said: I raided with my father in the summer campaign in the time of Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, under Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Malik, and we camped at Hisn Sinan, and people crowded the dwellings and cut off the roads. So my father stood among the people and said: O people, I raided with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in such-and-such a campaign, and people crowded the dwellings and cut off the roads, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a caller who called among the people: Whoever crowds a dwelling or cuts off a road, he has no jihad."
"1484","(2): Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri' Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun Abu Marhum narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives up fine clothing while able to afford it, out of humility for Allah, Allah will call him on the Day of Resurrection before all creation and give him choice among the garments of faith to wear whichever he wishes."
"1485","(3): Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives for Allah, withholds for Allah, loves for Allah, hates for Allah, and marries for Allah, has completed his faith."
"1486","(4): Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day voluntarily in the path of Allah, outside Ramadan, is distanced from Hell by a hundred years of travel at the pace of a trained, swift horse."
"1487","(5): al-Hakam ibn Musa Abu Salih narrated to us, Baqiyya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Hajjaj al-Mahri narrated to me, Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the Fajr prayer then sits remembering Allah until the sun rises, Paradise becomes due for him."
"1488","(6): Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to me, Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever eats food and says: Praise be to Allah who fed me this and provided me with it without any power or strength from me, he is forgiven his past sins; and whoever wears a garment and says: Praise be to Allah who clothed me with this and provided me with it without any power or strength from me, he is forgiven his past sins."
"1489","(7): Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever recites a thousand verses in the path of Allah, he will be recorded on the Day of Resurrection with the Prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous, and excellent are those as companions, if Allah wills."
"1490","(8): Muhriz narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever guards behind the Muslims voluntarily in the path of Allah, not compelled by a ruler, will not see Hell with his eye except the fulfillment of the oath, for Allah, glory be to Him, who has no partner, says: There is none of you but will pass over it."
"1491","(9): Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever steps over people's necks on Friday takes a bridge to Hell."
"1492","(10): Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us through it, Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade sitting in ih tiba posture (hugging the knees) on Friday while the imam is preaching."
"1493","(11): Abu Hammam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh al-Juhani, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the Qur'an and acts by what is in it, his parents will be dressed with a crown on the Day of Resurrection whose light is better than the light of the sun in the houses of this world were it among them; then what do you think of the one who acted by them."
"1494","(12): Abu Hammam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to me, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is dutiful to his parents, blessed is he; Allah will increase his lifespan."
"1495","(13): al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu al-Hajjaj al-Mahri narrated to me, Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the Fajr prayer then sits remembering Allah until the sun rises, Paradise becomes due for him."
"1496","(14): Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade sitting in ihtiba posture on Friday while the imam is preaching. Ibn al-Dawraqi said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It is not known among people, and people have continued to sit in ihtiba."
"1497","(15): Abu Abd Allah Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Marhum narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever suppresses anger while able to act upon it, Allah will call him before all witnesses on the Day of Resurrection and give him choice of whichever of the houris he wishes."
"1498","(16): Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Marhum narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats food then says: Praise be to Allah who fed me this food and provided me with it without any power or strength from me, he is forgiven his past sins; and whoever wears a garment and says: Praise be to Allah who clothed me with this and provided me with it without any power or strength from me, he is forgiven his past sins."
"1499","(17): Abu Abd Allah al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives up fine clothing while able to afford it, out of humility for Allah, Allah will call him on the Day of Resurrection before all creation until He gives him choice among the garments of faith to wear whichever he wishes."
"1500","(18): Abu Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives for Allah, withholds for Allah, loves for Allah, hates for Allah, and marries for Allah, has completed his faith."
"1501","Musnad of Arfaja ibn As'ad (1): Hawthara ibn Ashras Abu Amir narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab Ja'far ibn Hayyan informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tarafa ibn Arfaja ibn As'ad ibn Minqar - Abu Amir said: These are the maternal uncles of Banu Sa'd - that his grandfather Arfaja had his nose cut off in the pre-Islamic days on the day of al-Kulab, so he took a nose of silver, but it became foul upon him, so he mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered him to take a nose of gold. Abu Amir Hawthara said: And Abd al-Rahman claimed that he had seen his grandfather's nose."
"1502","(2): Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Tarafa ibn Arfaja narrated to us, and he claimed that he saw Arfaja his grandfather, he said: Arfaja's nose was cut off on the day of al-Kulab, so he took a nose of silver, but it became foul upon him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to take a nose of gold."
"1503","Musnad of Abi al-Ushara' al-Darimi (1): Ali ibn al-Ja'd, Hudba ibn Khalid, Abd al-A'la al-Narsi, Hawthara ibn Ashras, and Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abi al-Ushara', from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is slaughter only from the throat or the upper chest? He said: If you stabbed it in its thigh it would suffice you. Hawthara added: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, if you stabbed it in its thigh it would suffice you."
"1504","Musnad of Itban (1): Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, Mahmud ibn al-Rabi' narrated to me, from Itban ibn Malik, he said: I came to Madina and met Itban ibn Malik and said: A hadith reached me from you. He said: Something happened to my eyesight, so I sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I would love you to come to me and pray in my house so I may take it as a place of prayer. He said: So the Prophet came to me with whomever Allah willed of his Companions, and entered upon me while praying in my house, while his Companions were talking among themselves, then they attributed the bulk and worst of that to Malik ibn Dukhshum. He said: They wished he would supplicate against him so he would perish, and they wished some illness would befall him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer and said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: He says that, but it is not in his heart. He said: No one testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah and then enters Hell, or the Fire consumes him. He said: So this hadith pleased me, and I said to my son: Write it down, so he wrote it."
"1505","(2): Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from Itban ibn Malik, similar to it, with addition in it: And his Companions were talking among themselves, mentioning what they suffered from the hypocrites, then they attributed the bulk of that to Malik ibn Dukhshum. He said: They wished he would supplicate against him, blaming him for it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, and he mentioned similar to it."
"1506","(3): Abu Hamza Huraym ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughira, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from Itban ibn Malik, he said: I met Itban after that, and he narrated to me a hadith that pleased me, so I said to my son: Write it down, so he wrote it. He said: His eyesight had gone. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, if you came to me and prayed at my place in a spot I take as a mosque? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and began praying, while his Companions began talking. He said: They mentioned what they suffered of harm from the hypocrites, and laid the bulk of that upon Malik ibn al-Dukhshum, and they liked to urge the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to supplicate against him so he would perish. They said: O Prophet of Allah, part of his affair is such-and-such. He said: So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? They said: He only says that with his tongue, and it has no reality in his heart. He said: So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah and Allah will admit him to Hell - or he said: the Fire will ever consume him. Al-Mu'tamir said: I heard it from Anas, and he never narrated it to anyone."
"1507","Musnad of Amr ibn Kharija (1): Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Amr ibn Kharija, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed while upon a she-camel, while I was under its neck, and it was chewing its cud with its saliva flowing between my shoulders, and he said: O people, Allah has given every rightful one his right, so there is no bequest for an heir; the child is for the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone; whoever claims for other than his father, or affiliates to other than his masters out of dislike for them, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; Allah will not accept from him any exchange or recompense."
"1508","Musnad of Umara ibn Aws (1): Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, from Umara ibn Aws, who had prayed toward both qiblas, he said: While I was in my house, a caller called at the door: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has turned the qibla. So I testify concerning our imam, the men, the women, and the children, that they prayed toward here - meaning Bayt al-Maqdis - and toward here, meaning the Ka'ba."
"1509","Musnad of Sa'd ibn al-Atwal (1): Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Abd al-Malik Abu Ja'far informed us, from Abu Nadra, from Sa'd ibn al-Atwal, that a man died leaving three hundred dirhams and dependents. He said: So I wanted to spend it on his dependents, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother is detained because of his debt, so pay it off for him. So he paid it off for him, then said: O Messenger of Allah, I have paid off for him except for a woman who claimed two dinars, and she has no proof. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give her, for she is truthful."
"1510","(2): Ibn Abd Allah ibn Badr ibn Wasil ibn Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn al-Atwal narrated to us, he said: My father Abd Allah ibn Badr ibn Wasil ibn Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn al-Atwal narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn al-Atwal narrated to me, he said: Abd Allah ibn Sa'd used to go out to his companions at Tustar to visit them, staying the day of his arrival and the second, and leaving on the third. They would say to him: If only you stayed. He would say: I heard my father saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me - or I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding residence in the land of kharaj - for whoever resides in the land of kharaj has taken residence; so I dislike staying."
"1511","(3): Ibn Abd Allah ibn Badr narrated to us, Abbad ibn Musa al-Qurashi narrated to me, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Abd al-Malik Abu Ja'far, from Abu Nadra, from Sa'd ibn al-Atwal, that his father died leaving three hundred dirhams, dependents, and debt, so I wanted to spend on his dependents, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Your father is detained because of his debt, so pay it off for him. I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, I have paid off for him except a woman who claimed two dinars, and she has no proof. He said: Give her, for she is truthful, so I gave her."
"1512","(4): Ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Abbad ibn Musa narrated to me, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadra, from a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"1513","Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi (1): al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to me, he said: I heard Busr ibn Ubayd Allah - and once he said: from Busr ibn Ubayd Allah - from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Wathila ibn al-Asqa', from Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not sit upon graves, nor pray toward them."
"1514","Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari (1): Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Fadala ibn Husayn al-Attar narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Khattab ibn Sa'id, from Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Ansari, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those firmly rooted in mud, feeding in time of dearth; whoever sells them, their price is like ashes on a high peak that a wind blew and scattered."
"1515","(2): Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership."
"1516","al-Miqdad ibn Amr al-Kindi (1): Hudba narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Miqdad ibn Amr al-Kindi, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two men of my companions, and we sought whether anyone would host us, but no one hosted us. So we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, hunger and hardship have afflicted us, and we sought whether anyone would host us, but no one hosted us. So he gave us four goats and said: O Miqdad, take these and milk them, and divide into four parts: a part for me, a part for you, and a part for your two companions. So I used to do that. One night I drank my part, and my two companions drank their parts, and I put the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) part in the bowl and covered it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was detained. My soul said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been invited by a household of Madina and supped with them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has no need of this milk. My soul kept turning me until I went to the bowl and drank what was in it. When it settled in my belly, remorse, past and present, seized me. My soul said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will come hungry and thirsty, lift the bowl, and find nothing in it, and supplicate against you. So I covered myself as if asleep, though I was not asleep. The Messenger came and greeted with a greeting that let the awake hear without waking the sleeper. When he saw nothing in the bowl, he raised his head to the sky and said: O Allah, feed whoever fed us and give drink to whoever gave us drink. He said: So I seized the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), took the knife intending to slaughter one of those goats to feed him. I struck with my hand and it fell upon its udder, and behold it was full; then I looked at all of them, and behold they were full. So I milked into the bowl until it was full, then came to him smiling. He said: Some of your misdeeds, O Miqdad. I said: O Messenger of Allah, drink, then I will tell. So he drank, then I drank what remained, then told him. He said: O Miqdad, this is a blessing; you should have told me so we would wake our two companions and give them drink of this blessing. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when you have drunk the blessing, and I, I do not care whom it misses."
"1517","Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl al-Ansari (1): Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Zayd narrated to me, from Abu Sallam, from al-Hubrani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Recite the Qur'an, do not go to excess in it, do not turn away from it, do not eat by it, nor seek increase by it."
"1518","Musnad of Jundub ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali (1): Khalaf ibn al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Imran, from Jundub ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali - and I know he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: Recite the Qur'an as long as your hearts are united upon it; when you differ about it, stand up from it. He said: And in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I was a young boy near puberty."
"1519","(2): Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Suhayl, brother of Hazm, narrated to us, from Abu Imran, from Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever speaks about the Qur'an by his own opinion, even if right, has erred."
"1520","(3): Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Jundub and others, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam and Musa disputed; Musa said: You are Adam whom Allah created with His hand, made His angels prostrate to you, and settled you in His Paradise, yet you brought people out of Paradise? Adam said: You are Musa to whom Allah spoke privately and gave the Torah; do you blame me for a matter decreed upon me before He created me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So Adam overcame Musa; Adam overcame Musa."
"1521","(4): Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to me, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, Jundub ibn Sufyan, a man of Bajila, narrated to me, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a bringer of glad tidings came from a detachment he had sent, informing him of Allah's victory by which He aided his detachment and Allah's conquest He granted them. He said: O Messenger of Allah, while we were pursuing the enemy after Allah routed them, I caught up with a man with the sword; when he sensed the sword had reached him, he turned while fleeing and said: I am a Muslim, I am a Muslim, but I killed him, though he was, O Prophet of Allah, only seeking refuge. He said: So why did you not split open his heart and see whether he was truthful or lying? He said: Had I split open his heart, the heart would not inform me; is the heart anything but a lump of flesh? He said: So you killed him; you neither knew what was in his heart nor believed his tongue. He said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. He said: I will not seek forgiveness for you. They buried him, but he came to the surface of the earth three times. When his people saw that, they were ashamed and disgraced by what befell him, so they carried him and cast him into a ravine among those ravines."
"1522","(5): Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, Jundub ibn Sufyan, a man of Bajila, narrated to me, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a bringer of glad tidings came from a detachment he had sent, informing him of Allah's victory by which He aided his detachment and Allah's conquest He granted them, and he mentioned similar, with addition in it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said then: After me there will be tribulations like pieces of the dark night, striking like the striking of snakes and mature bulls; a man will wake in them a Muslim and evening a disbeliever, and evening in them a Muslim and morning a disbeliever. A man of the Muslims said: How should we act then, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Enter your houses and obscure your mention. A man of the Muslims said: What if one enters upon one of us in his house? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him hold his hand, and be the murdered servant of Allah, not the killing servant of Allah. For a man will be in the stronghold of Islam, then eat his brother's wealth, shed his blood, disobey his Lord, disbelieve in his Creator, and Hell becomes due for him."
"1523","(6): al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, he said: I heard Jundub al-Bajali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him; and whoever acts to be seen, Allah will show him."
"1524","(7): Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Umayr, from Jundub ibn Sufyan al-Bajali, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am your forerunner at the Hawd (Pool)."
"1525","(8): Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, al-Ansari narrated to us, al-Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Jundub ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the morning prayer is in Allah's protection; beware lest Allah demand you for anything of His protection."
"1526","(9): Abu Musa narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Hasan, he said: Jundub ibn Abd Allah narrated to us in this mosque, and we have forgotten nothing of it, nor do we fear he lied about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man among those before you developed an abscess, became distressed by it, took a knife and cut his hand with it, and the blood did not stop until he died. Allah Almighty said: My servant hastened to Me with himself; I have forbidden Paradise to him. Abu Musa said: Wahb said: The Qadariyya argue by this hadith, but they have no proof in it."
"1527","(10): Abu Musa narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abu Hurayra - this chain is incomplete in the printed source and its matn follows in the next report."
"1528","(10) (m): And from Hammad, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Jundub ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Adam met Musa; Musa said: You are Adam whom Allah created with His hand, settled you in His Paradise, and made His angels prostrate to you; you did what you did and brought your offspring out of Paradise? Adam said: O Musa, are you the one whom Allah chose with His message, spoke to, and brought near as a confidant? He said: Yes. He said: Am I older, or the remembrance? He said: The remembrance. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So Adam overcame Musa; Adam overcame Musa."
"1529","(11): Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Jundub ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man said: By Allah, Allah will not forgive so-and-so. So Allah said: Who is it who swears upon Me that I will not forgive so-and-so? I have forgiven so-and-so and annulled your deed."
"1530","(12): Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Humayd, meaning al-Ru'asi, narrated to us, Hasan ibn Salih narrated to me, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever of Allah's creation greets you, return it, even if he is a Magian, for Allah says: And when you are greeted with a greeting, greet with better than it or return it."
"1531","(13): Ishaq narrated to us, Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan: And when you are greeted with a greeting, greet with better than it - for the people of Islam - or return it - to the people of polytheism."
"1532","(14): Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Jundub ibn Sufyan, he said: We prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and people slaughtered their sacrifices before the prayer. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished and saw them having slaughtered before the prayer, he said: Whoever slaughtered his sacrifice before the prayer, let him slaughter another slaughter; and whoever did not slaughter until we prayed, let him slaughter upon Allah's name."
"1533","(15): Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from al-Aswad, from Jundub ibn Sufyan al-Bajali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - his finger bled in one of the battle scenes - and he said: Are you but a finger that bled, and in Allah's path what you suffered."
"1534","(16): Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, from a companion of his, who is al-Hadrami, from Abi al-Sawwar narrating from Jundub ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a party and appointed over them Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah. When he set out to go, he wept out of longing for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sent in his place a man called Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, wrote him a letter, and ordered him not to compel any of his companions to march with him. When he read the letter, he said: We hear and obey - meaning Allah and His Messenger - informed them of the news and read them the letter. Two men returned, and the rest went on. They met Ibn al-Hadrami and killed him, without realizing whether that day was of Rajab or Jumada. The polytheists said to the Muslims: You did such-and-such in the sacred month. They came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him the story, so Allah revealed: They ask you about the sacred month, fighting in it; say: Fighting in it is grave - up to His saying - and trial (shirk) is greater than killing. He said: Shirk. Some of those in the detachment said: By Allah, only one killed him; if it be good, I have undertaken it, and if it be a sin, I have done it. Some Muslims said: If they incurred no sin in this month of theirs, they have no reward in it. So Allah revealed: Those who believed, emigrated, and strove in Allah's path, those hope for Allah's mercy, and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful."
"1535","Musnad of Thabit ibn al-Dahhak (1): Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, that Abu Qilaba narrated to him, that Thabit ibn al-Dahhak narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears falsely upon a religion other than Islam is as he said; a man has no vow concerning what he does not own."
"1536","Musnad of Hamza al-Aslami (1): Sa'id ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, al-Mughira ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid ibn Hizam al-Hizami narrated to us, Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, that Muhammad ibn Hamza narrated to him, from his father Hamza al-Aslami, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him in a detachment and put him in command over them, and said: If you capture so-and-so, burn him with fire. When I turned, he called me from behind, so I came. He said: If you capture so-and-so, kill him and do not burn him with fire, for none punishes with fire but the Lord of Fire."
"1537","Yazid ibn Rukana (1): Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Sa'id, Abd Allah ibn Yazid ibn Rukana narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that he divorced his wife irrevocably, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What did you intend by it? He said: One. He said: By Allah? He said: By Allah. He said: It is upon what you intended."
"1538","(2): Shayban narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Sa'id al-Hashimi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Ali ibn Yazid ibn Rukana, from his father, from his grandfather, that he divorced his wife irrevocably in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: What did you intend by that? He said: One. He said: By Allah? He said: By Allah. He said: It is upon what you intended."
"1539","al-Jarud (1): Hudba narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The stray of a Muslim is the burning of Hell."
"1540","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi (1): Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr informed me, that Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Hadrami narrated to him, that Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' al-Zubaydi narrated to him, that he passed with a companion of his by Umm Ayman, while youths of Quraysh had loosened their waist-wrappers, made them into whips to strike with, while naked. Abd Allah said: When we passed them, they said: These are priests, leave them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out upon them; when they saw him they scattered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned angry until he entered, while I was behind the room. I heard him saying: Glory be to Allah; they neither felt shame before Allah nor concealed themselves from His Messenger. Umm Ayman was with him, saying: Seek forgiveness for them, O Messenger of Allah. Abd Allah said: May my father be ransom, he did not seek forgiveness for them."
"1541","(2): Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fadala narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'a, from Sulayman ibn Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn Jaz', he said: We ate with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day roast meat while in the mosque; the prayer was established, and we did no more than wipe our hands with pebbles."
"1542","Hubayb ibn Mughaffal (1): Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: And Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu Imran, from Hubayb ibn Mughaffal, that he saw Muhammad ibn Ulba al-Qurashi dragging his waist-wrapper. Hubayb ibn Mughfil looked at him and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever treads it arrogantly, treads it into Hell."
"1543","Musnad of Abi Shahm (1): Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata' narrated to us, from Bayan ibn Bishr, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abi Shahm - and he was a horseman - he said: A slave-girl passed by me on one of the roads of Madina, and I reached with my hand to her waist. The next day people came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledging allegiance, and I came and extended my hand to pledge, but he withdrew his hands and said: Are you the man of the little colocynth yesterday? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge me; I will never return. He said: Then yes."
"1544","Musnad of Rafi' ibn Makith (1): Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Uthman ibn Zufar, from some of the sons of Rafi' ibn Makith, from Rafi' ibn Makith - who had witnessed al-Hudaybiyya - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Good ownership is growth, and bad character is ill omen."
"1545","(2): Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Amir ibn Abi Umayya, brother of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub (in major impurity) and fast without breaking."
"1546","Musnad of Rabah ibn Rabi' (1): Sa'id ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us at Basra, al-Mughira ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hizami narrated to us, Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from Muraqqi' ibn Sayfi, from his grandfather Rabah ibn Rabi', he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a campaign, with Khalid ibn al-Walid at the vanguard of the people, when a slain woman was found on the road, people marveling at her form, struck by the vanguard. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, stood over her, and said: Ha, she was not one to fight. Then he said to a man: Catch up with Khalid; let him not kill offspring, nor a hireling."
"1547","Musnad of Afif al-Kindi (1): Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali narrated to us, from Asad ibn Wada'a al-Bajali, from Ibn Yahya ibn Afif al-Kindi, from his father, from his grandfather Afif, he said: I came in the pre-Islamic days to Makka intending to buy for my family its garments and perfume. I came to al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who was a merchant, while I was sitting with him looking at the Ka'ba, the sun high in the sky. I had just gone when a youth came, cast his gaze to the sky, then stood facing the qibla. Only a little passed until a boy came and stood on his right; only a little passed until a woman came and stood behind them. The youth bowed, and the boy and woman bowed; the youth rose, and the boy and woman rose. I said: O Abbas, a momentous matter! Abbas said: A momentous matter. Do you know who this youth is? I said: No. He said: This is Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, my brother's son. Do you know who this boy is? This is Ali, my brother's son. Do you know who this woman is? This is Khadija bint Khuwaylid, his wife. This brother's son of mine informed me that his Lord, Lord of the heavens and earth, ordered him with this religion he follows; and by Allah, there is no one on the whole earth upon this religion but these three."
"1548","Musnad of Qatada ibn al-Nu'man (1): Abu Ma'mar al-Hudhali Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'sa'a, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: My brother Qatada ibn al-Nu'man informed me that a man stood in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in the pre-dawn: Say, He is Allah, One, repeating it, adding nothing to it. In the morning a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so stood tonight reciting in the pre-dawn: Say, He is Allah, One; Allah, the Eternal; He neither begets nor is born; and there is none like unto Him, repeating it, adding nothing, as if the man deemed it little. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, it equals a third of the Qur'an."
"1549","(2): Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn Ghusayl narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada, from his father, meaning from Qatada ibn al-Nu'man, that his eye was struck on the day of Badr, its pupil flowing upon his cheek. They wanted to cut it, but he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: No. He called for him, pressed his pupil with his palm, and it could not be known which of his eyes was struck."
"1550","(3): Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Adhrami narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ubayd, from his grandfather, he said: The eye of Abu Dharr was struck on the day of Uhud, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in it, and it became his soundest eye."
"1551","Musnad of Ma'n ibn Yazid (1): Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam and others said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abi al-Juwayriya, from Ma'n ibn Yazid, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and my father and my grandfather, disputed to him and he ruled for me, and he addressed (proposed marriage) for me and married me. Ma'n said: Spoils are not lawful until divided among people as one lot; when divided, it is lawful for me to give you. This is the wording of Abd al-A'la only, and in the hadith of others there is not: then when divided, I give you."
"1552","Musnad of Ahmar (1): Abu Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan saying: Ahmar, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to us, he said: We used to shelter the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from how he kept his elbows away from his sides when prostrating."
"1553","(2): Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Amir, he said: The Ansar came on the day of Uhud and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have wounds and hardship; how do you command us? He said: Dig, widen, and put two or three men in the grave. They said: Whom shall we present? He said: Present the most versed of them in the Qur'an. He said: So my father was presented before two of the Ansar - or he said: one of the Ansar."
"1554","(3): Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, he said: People used to buy gold with silver on credit - Isma'il said: I think until the stipend - then Hisham ibn Amir came upon them and forbade them, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us selling gold on credit, and informed us - or he said: told us - that that is riba."
"1555","(4): Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from some of their elders, he said: Hisham ibn Amir said to his neighbors: You pass by to men who were no closer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than I, nor more retentive of his hadith than I; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Between the creation of Adam until the Hour comes, there is no creation greater than the Dajjal."
"1556","(5): Zuhayr narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from a group of them, among them Abu al-Dahma' and Abu Qatada, he said: We used to pass Hisham, going to Imran ibn Husayn, and one day he said: You pass me by to men who were no closer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than I, nor more knowledgeable of his hadith than I; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Between the creation of Adam until the Hour stands, there is no creation greater than the Dajjal."
"1557","(6): Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mu'adha, from Hisham ibn Amir al-Ansari, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott a Muslim for more than three days; both deviate from truth while upon their boycott; the first of them to return, his hastening with return is expiation for him; if he greets him and he does not accept his greeting, the angels return it upon him and Satan returns upon the other; if they die upon their boycott, they will not enter Paradise, or will not gather in Paradise."
"1558","(7): Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abi al-Dahma', from Hisham ibn Amir, he said: They complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of their wounds, and he said: Dig, do well, widen, bury two and three in the grave, and present the most versed of them in the Qur'an. He said: So my father died and was presented before two men."
"1559","Musnad of Abi Jum'a (1): Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Utarid al-Basri narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Asid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Salih ibn Jubayr, from Abi Jum'a, he said: I lunched with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with us Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah. Abu Ubayda said to him: O Messenger of Allah, is anyone better than us? We embraced Islam with you and strove with you. He said: Yes; a people after me who believe in me without having seen me."
"1560","(2): Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Sa'id, mawla of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, from Abi Khalaf, from Abd Allah ibn Awf, he said: I heard Aba Jum'a Junbudh ibn Sab' saying: I fought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the start of the day as a disbeliever, and fought with him at the end of the day as a Muslim; we were three men and seven women, and concerning us was revealed: And were it not for believing men and believing women - the verse."
"1561","(3): Abu Ubayda ibn al-Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, Abu Sa'id, mawla of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abd Allah, he said: I met an old man in Sham and said: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; I heard him saying: O Allah, forgive us and have mercy on us."
"1562","(4): al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Mushir ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Sal' narrated to us, my father informed me, he said: I said to Abd Khayr: How old are you? He said: One hundred and twenty years. I said: Do you remember anything of the pre-Islamic affair? He said: Yes; we were in the land of Yemen, and the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us calling people to abundant good. My father was among those who went out while I was a boy. When my father returned he said to my mother: Order this pot to be poured out for the dogs, for we have embraced Islam, so embrace Islam."
"1563","Musnad of Abd Allah ibn Sarjis (1): Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Sarjis, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ate with him bread and meat - or he said: tharid. I said: May Allah forgive you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And you. I said to Abd Allah ibn Sarjis: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seek forgiveness for you? He said: Yes, and for you, and he recited this verse: And seek forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and women. He said: Then I circled until I stood behind him and saw the seal of prophethood at the cartilage of his left shoulder, a collection with moles upon it."
"1564","(2): Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Sarjis narrated to us, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man washing with a woman's leftover, and a woman washing with a man's leftover; rather both draw from it together."
"1565","Musnad of Amr ibn Murra (1): Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Abi Hasan: that Amr ibn Murra said to Mu'awiya: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no ruler who closes his door before those of need and want, but Allah closes the doors of heaven before his need and destitution."
"1566","(2): Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, he said: Abu Hasan narrated to me, from Amr ibn Murra, he said: I said to Mu'awiya: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no commander or ruler who closes his door before those of need, want, and destitution, but Allah closes the doors of heaven before his need and destitution. He said: So Mu'awiya appointed a man over people's needs."
"1567","(3): Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Sabra narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra al-Juhani, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Whoever here is of Ma'add, let him stand. He said: So I took my garment to stand. He said: Sit. Then he said a second time, and I said: Of whom am I, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Of Himyar."
"1568","Mukhawwal (1): Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Mukhawwal al-Bahzi, then al-Sulami, saying: I heard my father - who had lived through the pre-Islamic days and Islam - saying: I set snares of mine at al-Abwa', and a gazelle fell into one rope but escaped. I went out after it and found a man who had taken it. We disputed over it and brought each other to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We found him camped at al-Abwa' under a tree, shading himself with leather. We disputed to him, and he judged it between us in halves. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we meet camels with milk while tied, and we are needy. He said: Call the camels' owner three times; if he comes, else untie their ties, then drink, then tie, and leave for the milk its causes. I said: O Messenger of Allah, stray animals come to us; do we have reward for watering them? He said: Yes; in every moist liver is reward. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began narrating to us, he said: There will come upon people a time when the best wealth in it is sheep between the two mosques, eating trees and coming to water; its owner eats of its young, drinks of its milk, wears of its wool - or he said: its hair - while tribulations plunge among the roots of the Arabs. By Allah, you do not care - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it three times. I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Establish prayer, give zakat, fast Ramadan, perform Hajj of the House and Umra, be dutiful to your parents, join kinship, honor the guest, command good, forbid evil, and stay with truth wherever it turns."
"1569","Musnad of the uncle of Abi Hurra al-Raqashi (1): Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abi Hurra al-Raqashi, from his uncle, he said: I was holding the halter of the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) she-camel in the middle days of Tashriq in the Farewell Hajj, and he said among what he said: O people, all riba is abolished; the first riba abolished is the riba of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib: You shall have your capitals; you do no wrong, nor are you wronged."
"1570","(2): Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abi Hurra al-Raqashi, from his uncle, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wealth of a Muslim man is not lawful except with his willing consent."
"1571","al-Harith al-Ash'ari (1): Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, that Zayd narrated to him, that Abu Sallam narrated to him, that al-Harith al-Ash'ari narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah commanded Yahya ibn Zakariyya with five words to act by and to order the Children of Isra'il to act by; and Isa son of Maryam said to him: Allah commanded you with five words to act by and to order the Children of Isra'il to act by; either you order them, or I order them? He said: If you precede me with them, I fear to be punished or swallowed. He said: So he gathered people in Bayt al-Maqdis until it filled, people sitting on balconies. He said: So he admonished them. He said: Allah commanded me with five words to act by and I order you to act by: first, to worship Allah and associate nothing with Him; the likeness of one who associates with Allah is like a man who bought a slave from his pure wealth with gold or silver, saying: This is my house and this is my work, so work and render to me - but he works and renders to other than his master; which of you would like his slave to be so? Allah created you and provided you, so associate nothing with Him; He ordered you with prayer, so when you pray do not turn away; He ordered you with fasting, and its likeness is like a man with a purse of musk among a band, all loving to find its scent, and fasting is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk; I order you with charity, and its likeness is like a man captured by the enemy who stood to him, binding his hand to his neck, and he said: Will you let me ransom myself from you? He said: So he kept giving them little and much to free himself from them; I order you to remember Allah much, and its likeness is like a man pursued swiftly by the enemy until he came to a fortified fortress and secured himself in it; likewise the servant secures himself from Satan only by Allah's remembrance. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I order you with five Allah ordered me with: the community, hearing, obedience, emigration, and jihad in Allah's path. Whoever leaves the community a handspan, Islam is cast from his head unless he returns; whoever calls with the call of ignorance is of the heaps of Hell. It was said: Even if he fasted and prayed? He said: Even if he prayed and fasted; so call with Allah's call by which He named you: Muslims, believers, servants of Allah."
"1572","Musnad of Abi Hubayra al-Ansari (1): Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Makhrama informed us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Nafi', he said: Abu Hubayra al-Ansari, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saw me praying Duha when the sun had risen, rebuked me for that and forbade me, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pray until the sun rises high, for it rises in the horn of Satan."
"1573","Musnad of Sa'd, mawla of Abu Bakr (1): Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sa'd, mawla of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to Abu Bakr - while Sa'd was his slave, and his service pleased the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free Sa'd. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, we have none here but him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free Sa'd; men will come to you, men will come to you."
"1574","(2): Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sa'd, he said: I brought dates before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they began pairing (eating two together). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade pairing."
"1575","(3): Abu Hisham narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Daghfal: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died at sixty-five."
"1576","Ubayd, mawla of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (1): Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Ubayd, mawla of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Two fasting women used to backbite people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a bowl and said to them: Vomit. So they vomited pus, blood, and fresh flesh. Then he said: These two fasted from the lawful and broke fast upon the unlawful."
"1577","Abu Malik al-Ash'ari (1): Hudba narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, that Zayd narrated to him, that Abu Sallam narrated to him, that Abu Malik al-Ash'ari narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four in my nation are of pre-Islamic affair they will not leave: boasting of lineages, reviling genealogies, seeking rain by stars, and wailing. And he said: The wailing woman, if she does not repent before her death, will be raised on the Day of Resurrection wearing a garment of tar and a coat of mange."
"1578","Musnad of al-Abbas ibn Mirdas al-Sulami (1): Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Abd al-Qahir ibn al-Sari al-Sulami narrated to us, Ibn Kinana ibn al-Abbas ibn Mirdas al-Sulami narrated to me, that his father narrated to him, from his father al-Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated on the evening of Arafa for his nation for forgiveness and mercy, supplicating much. Allah answered him: I have done and forgiven your nation except the wrong of some against others. He repeated, saying: O Lord, You are able to forgive the wrongdoer and reward the wronged better than his grievance. That evening there was only that. Next day he supplicated in the morning of Muzdalifa, repeating supplication for his nation. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) soon smiled. Some Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom, you smiled at an hour you did not laugh in; what made you laugh, may Allah make your tooth laugh? He said: I smiled at Allah's enemy Iblis when he knew Allah answered me concerning my nation and forgave the wrongdoer; he fell to calling with ruin and woe, throwing dust upon his head. Once he said: So I laughed at his distress."
"1579","(2): Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abi al-Huwayrith, that he heard al-Hakam ibn Mina', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar: Gather for me whoever here is of Quraysh. So he gathered them, then said: O Messenger of Allah, do you go out to them or do they enter? He said: Rather I go out to them. So he went out and said: O assembly of Quraysh, is there among you other than you? They said: No, except sons of our sisters. He said: The son of a people's sister is of them. Then he said: O assembly of Quraysh, know that the nearest people to the Prophet are the God-fearing; see, let not people come with deeds on the Day of Resurrection while you come with worldliness carrying it, so I turn my face from you. Then he recited: Indeed the nearest people to Ibrahim are those who followed him, this Prophet, those who believed, and Allah is guardian of believers."
"1580","Musnad of Umayr ibn Sa'd (1): Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Abu Talha al-Khawlani, he said: We came to Umayr ibn Sa'd among a group of people of Palestine - called the unique peer - and sat on a great bench of his in his house. He said to his slave: O slave, water the horses. In the house was a stone basin. So he watered them. He said: Where is so-and-so? He said: She is mangy, dripping blood - or he said: dripping water - Abu Ishaq doubted. He said: Water her. One of the people said: Then all horses will get mange. He said: Water her, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No contagion, no omen, no hama. Did you not see the camel among camels in the desert, then morning finds a spot in its chest or flanks not there before; who infected the first?"
"1581","Musnad of al-Harith ibn Wuqaysh (1): Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Qays, from al-Harith ibn Wuqaysh, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No two Muslims between whom four die but Allah admits them to Paradise by His mercy. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, and three? He said: And three. He said: And two? He said: And two. He said: And of my nation is one by whose intercession more than Mudar will enter."
"1582","Habba ibn Habis al-Tamimi (1): Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, Yahya narrated to me, he said: Habba ibn Habis al-Tamimi narrated to me, that his father informed him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is nothing in hama; the evil eye is true; the truest of omens is good omen."
"1583","al-Falatan ibn Asim (1): Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, meaning from al-Falatan ibn Asim, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when revelation descended upon him. When it descended, his gaze stayed fixed with eyes open, his hearing and heart freed for what comes to him from Allah. He said: We knew that of him. He said to the scribe: Write: Not equal are the sitting of the believers and the striving in Allah's path. The blind man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is our fault? Then Allah revealed, and we said to the blind man: It is being revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He feared something of his affair was being revealed, so he remained standing, saying: I seek refuge from the anger of the Messenger of Allah. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the scribe: Write: Except those of harm."
"1584","Musnad of Ma'n ibn Nadla (1): Abu Musa Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ma'n narrated to us, my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ma'n narrated to me, from his father Ma'n ibn Nadla, that Nadla met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Marrayn with milking she-camels of his. He milked for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) into a vessel, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, then drank from one vessel, then said: O Messenger of Allah, by Him who sent you with truth, I used to drink seven and neither satisfy nor fill. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer drinks in one intestine, and the disbeliever drinks in seven intestines."
"1585","(2): Abu Ya'la informed us, Ibn al-Madini narrated it to us with its chain, similar to it."
"1586","Musnad of Wabisa ibn Ma'bad (1): Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Salam, from Ayyub ibn Abd Allah ibn Mikraz, from Wabisa ibn Ma'bad al-Asadi, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intending to leave nothing of righteousness and sin but ask him. I came to him among a group asking him fatwa. I began stepping over them. They said: Away, O Wabisa, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Leave me to draw near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for he is the dearest people for me to draw near. He said: Leave Wabisa; draw near, O Wabisa. Ask your heart, ask yourself; ask your heart, ask yourself. Righteousness is what the soul is tranquil with and the heart tranquil with; sin is what wavers in the soul and hesitates in the chest, even if people give you fatwa and give you fatwa - three times."
"1587","(2): Ali ibn Hamza al-Mi'wali narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from al-Zubayr Abu Abd al-Salam, from Ayyub ibn Abd Allah, from Wabisa al-Asadi, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intending to leave nothing of righteousness and sin but ask him of it. I came while around him a group of Muslims asking him fatwa. I began stepping over them to him. They said: Away, O Wabisa. I said to them: Leave me to draw near him, for he is the dearest people for me to draw near. He said: Leave Wabisa; draw near, O Wabisa; draw near, O Wabisa. So I drew near and sat before him. He said to me: O Wabisa, do you ask me or shall I tell you? I said: Rather tell me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You came to ask me of righteousness and sin? I said: Yes. He gathered his fingers, then began tapping my chest with them, saying: O Wabisa, ask your heart, ask yourself; ask your heart, ask yourself. Righteousness is what the soul is tranquil with; sin is what wavers in the chest, even if people give you fatwa and give you fatwa - three times."
"1588","(3): Abu Ubayda ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, Malik ibn Su'ayr narrated to us, al-Sari ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Wabisa ibn Ma'bad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned while a man was praying behind the rows, and said: O praying one alone, did you not join a row and enter with them, or drag a man to you if the place was tight for you? Repeat your prayer, for you have no prayer."
"1589","(4): Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi al-Raqqi narrated to us, Asbugh ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Shaddad, mawla of Iyad, from Wabisa - Abu Uthman Amr said: meaning Ibn Ma'bad, if Allah wills - that he used to stand among people on the day of Adha or Fitr, saying: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj, saying: What day is this? People said: The day of sacrifice. He said: What month is this? Then he said: What land is this? They said: This town. He said: Your blood, wealth, and honors are forbidden to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours, until the day you meet Him. Then he said: O Allah, have I conveyed? Let the witness convey the absent. Wabisa said: We testify against you as was testified against us."
"1590","(5): Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid said: Abu Salama al-Khuza'i narrated to us, that Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated to them in this hadith, that Salim ibn Wabisa led them in prayer at al-Raqqa and mentioned this hadith of Wabisa, and Wabisa said: We testify against you as was testified against us; you have retained and we convey to you."
"1591","(6): Abu Ali Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us, Abu Fadala Faraj ibn Fadala narrated to us, from Abd al-Khabir ibn Qays ibn Thabit ibn Shammas, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: On the day of Qurayza a man of the Ansar called Khallad was killed. His mother was told: O Umm Khallad, Khallad was killed. She came veiled. She was told: Khallad was killed, yet you come to us veiled? She said: If I am bereaved of Khallad, I will not be bereaved of my modesty. They mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: He has the reward of two martyrs. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, why? He said: Because the People of the Book killed him."
"1592","Musnad of Safina (a man) (1): Zahmawayh narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, Hajib, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us, he said: I entered with al-Hakam al-A'raj upon Bakr ibn Abd Allah, and they discussed the dead punished by the living's weeping. Bakr narrated to us, he said: A man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us - while Abu Hurayra opposed him in that - he said: Abu Hurayra said: By Allah, if a man went out fighting in Allah's path, then was killed as a martyr in a region of the earth's regions, then a woman foolishly or ignorantly wept over him, this martyr would be punished by this foolish woman's weeping over him. A man said: The Messenger of Allah spoke truth and Abu Hurayra lied; the Messenger of Allah spoke truth and Abu Hurayra lied."
"1593","A man (1): Zahmawayh narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from some Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a deed to enter Paradise, without much upon me. He said: Do not anger."
"1594","A man from his father (1): Zahmawayh narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, Abu Janab Yahya ibn Abi Hayya narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from a man, from his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My brother is ill. He said: What is your brother's ailment? He said: Madness. He said: Send him to me. He said: So he came and sat before him. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited over him the Opening of the Book, four verses from the start of Surat al-Baqara, two verses from its middle: And your god is one God; there is no god but He, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful - Indeed in the creation of the heavens and earth - until finishing the verse, Ayat al-Kursi, three verses from the end of Surat al-Baqara, a verse from the start of Surat Al Imran: Allah testifies there is no god but He, the angels and those of knowledge, upholding justice - to the end of the verse, a verse from Surat al-A'raf: Indeed your Lord is Allah who created the heavens and earth, a verse from Surat al-Mu'minun: So exalted is Allah, the True King; there is no god but He, Lord of the Noble Throne, a verse from Surat al-Jinn: And that exalted is the majesty of our Lord; He has taken neither wife nor son, ten verses from the start of Surat al-Saff, three verses from the end of Surat al-Hashr, and Say, He is Allah, One, and the two refuge-seeking chapters."
"1595","(2): Zahmawayh narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn Dinar, mawla of the family of al-Zubayr, a trustworthy one informed me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar intercourse with pregnant women, saying: Would you water another's crop?"
"1596","Farwah ibn Nawfal al-Ashjai (1596): Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Farwah ibn Nawfal, who said: I came to Madinah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What has brought you? I said: That you teach me words to say when I take my bed. He said: Recite 'Say: O disbelievers,' for it is a declaration of freedom from shirk."
"1597","The messenger of Caesar (1597): Hawtharah ibn Ashras narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Abi Rashid, who said: The messenger of Caesar was my neighbor in the time of Yazid ibn Muawiyah, and I said to him: Tell me about the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Caesar. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Dihyah al-Kalbi to Caesar, and wrote with him a letter giving him the choice of one of three: either to accept Islam and keep what is in his hands of his kingdom, or to pay the kharaj (tribute), or to permit war. He said: So Caesar gathered his patricians and priests in his palace and locked the door upon them, and said: Muhammad has written to me giving me the choice of one of three: either I accept Islam and keep what is in my hands of my kingdom, or I pay the tribute, or I permit war, and you find in what you read of your books that he will possess what is under my feet of my kingdom. So they snorted a snort until some of them came out of their hooded cloaks, and said: Do you send to a man of the Arabs who came in his two garments and sandals with tribute? He said: Be silent; I only wanted to know your holding to your religion and your desire for it. Then he said: Seek for me a man of the Arabs, so they brought me, and he wrote with me a letter to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said to me: Watch what falls from his speech, and do not let fall what is said at the mention of night and day. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was with his companions, sitting on their haunches with the straps of their swords around them near the well of Tabuk. I said: Which of you is Muhammad? He gestured with his hand toward himself, so I handed him the letter, and he handed it to a man beside him. I said: Who is this? They said: Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Muawiyah, answer him about his letter. So Muawiyah wrote the reply, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sealed it, then said: Carry it to your master. So I carried it until I came to him, and he read it, and I memorized what was in it as I memorize the night and the day."
"1598","Urwah ibn Masud (1598): Hawtharah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, that Urwah ibn Masud al-Thaqafi said to his people in the time of al-Hudaybiyah: O my people, I have seen kings and spoken to them, so send me to Muhammad and I will speak to him. So he came to him at al-Hudaybiyah, and Urwah began speaking to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and touching the beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while al-Mughirah ibn Shubah stood armed at the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Mughirah said to him: Withhold your hand before it does not return to you. Urwah raised his head and said: Is it you? By Allah, you are still in your treachery; you have not come out of it yet. Then Urwah returned to his people and said: O my people, I have seen kings and spoken to them; I have never seen the like of Muhammad at all. He is not a king, and I saw the sacrificial animals held back, eating their own hair, and I do not see but that a calamity will strike you. So he turned away, he and those of his people with him, and climbed the wall of Taif, and testified that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. A man of his people shot him with an arrow and killed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Praise be to Allah who has placed in my ummah the like of the companion of Ya-Sin."
"1599","Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir (1599): Hawtharah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque while he was standing, and his chest had a sound like the sound of a boiling pot."
"1600","Abu al-Jad (1600): Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami informed me, from Abu al-Jad al-Damri, who was a companion, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever abandons Friday prayer three times out of negligence toward it, Allah seals his heart."
"1601","A man (1601): Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, that a man in Kufah testified that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed as a martyr, so the guards seized him and brought him to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Had you not forbidden us, or had you not forbidden us to kill anyone, we would have killed him; this one claims that he testifies that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed as a martyr. The man said to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: And you testify; do you remember that I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, and he gave me, and I came to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him, and he gave me, and I came to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him, and he gave me, and I came to Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him, and he gave me. He said: Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to bless me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How would you not be blessed when a Prophet gave you, and a Siddiq, and two martyrs; and a Prophet gave you, and a Siddiq and two martyrs; and a Prophet gave you, and a Siddiq and two martyrs?"
"1602","Musnad of Ammar ibn Yasir (1602): Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us in the year 306, al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Warraq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hazawwar, who said: I heard Abu Maryam al-Thaqafi say: I heard Ammar ibn Yasir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to Ali: O Ali, glad tidings to whoever loves you and is truthful concerning you, and woe to whoever hates you and lies concerning you."
"1603","(1603): Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Fadl al-Anazi narrated to us, from Ismail al-Ijli, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ammar, Jibril came to me just now, and I said: O Jibril, tell me of the virtues of Umar ibn al-Khattab in heaven. He said: O Muhammad, if I were to tell you of the virtues of Umar for as long as Nuh remained among his people, a thousand years less fifty, the virtues of Umar would not be exhausted; and Umar is indeed a good deed among the good deeds of Abu Bakr."
"1604","(1604): Harun ibn Maruf and Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, that Hassan ibn Bilal al-Muzani told him that he saw Ammar ibn Yasir perform ablution and pass his fingers through his beard. It was said to him: Do you do this? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do it."
"1605","(1605): Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Najiyah ibn Kab, that Ammar said to Umar: Do you remember when I and you were with the camels, and I became junub, so I rolled in the dust as an animal rolls, then I met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Tayammum would have sufficed you for that."
"1606","(1606): Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Malik, and Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, who said: We were with Umar when a man came to him and said: O Commander of the Believers, we stay a month and two months without finding water. Umar said: As for me, I would not pray until I find water. Ammar said: O Commander of the Believers, do you remember when we were at such and such a place herding camels, and we recalled that we had become junub. He said: Yes, and I rolled in the dust, then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him. He laughed and said: Clean earth would have sufficed you. And he struck the earth with his palms, then blew into them, then wiped his face and part of his forearms. He said: Fear Allah, O Ammar. He said: O Commander of the Believers, if you wish I will never mention it as long as I live. He said: No, but we entrust you with what you have taken charge of."
"1607","(1607): Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Dharr, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab and Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: A man asked Umar: I became junub and did not find water? He said: Do not pray. Ammar said: Do you not remember that I and you were in a detachment in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and became junub; as for you, you did not pray, and as for me, I rolled in the dust and prayed. Then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: It would have sufficed you. And he struck the earth with his hand, blew into his palms, and wiped his face and hands."
"1608","(1608): Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Azrah, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ammar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him in tayammum with the hands and the face."
"1609","(1609): Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, that Ammar ibn Yasir said: We performed tayammum with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we wiped our faces and our hands up to the shoulders with dust."
"1610","(1610): Bundar narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ghundar, narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Salamah say: I saw Ammar ibn Yasir on the day of Siffin as an old man, tall, dark, holding a spear in his hand while his hand trembled, and he said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, I fought with this banner with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three times, and this is the fourth. By Him in whose hand is my soul, if they struck us until they brought us to the lote-trees of Hajar, we would know that our righteous ones are upon the truth and that they are upon misguidance."
"1611","(1611): Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Thabit ibn Hammad Abu Zayd narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ammar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was watering a camel of mine, and I spat, and my spit hit my garment, so I began washing my garment with the water-skin before me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ammar, your spit and your tears are only like the water in your water-skin; you only wash your garment of urine, feces, semen, of the major fluid, blood, and vomit."
"1612","(1612): It was read to Bishr ibn al-Walid while I was present: Abu Yusuf narrated to us, from Abu Hanifah, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Ibn al-Hawtakiyyah, from Umar: that a man asked him about eating rabbit? He said: Call Ammar for me. So Ammar came, and he said: Tell us the hadith of the rabbit on the day we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in such and such a place. Ammar said: A Bedouin gifted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a rabbit, and he ordered the people to eat. A Bedouin said: I saw blood. He said: It is nothing. Then he said: Come near and eat. He said: I am fasting. He said: What fast? He said: I fast three days of every month. He said: Why have you not made them the white days?"
"1613","(1613): Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Bakhtari, that Ammar was brought a drink of milk, and he laughed. It was said to him: What makes you laugh? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last drink you drink will be milk when you die."
"1614","(1614): Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, from a freedwoman of Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: Ammar fell ill with an illness that weighed heavily on him, and he lost consciousness. He awoke while we were weeping around him, and said: What makes you weep? Do you fear that I will die on my bed? My beloved (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that the rebellious party will kill me, and that my last provision will be a sip of milk."
"1615","(1615): Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, Said al-Maqburi narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from his father: that Ammar ibn Yasir prayed two rakahs, and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith said to him: O Abu al-Yaqzan, I see you have made them light. He said: I hastened with them against whispering; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man prays prayer and perhaps he has of it only its tenth, or its ninth, or its eighth, or its seventh, or its sixth, or its fifth, until he went through the number."
"1616","(1616): Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, who said: I heard Qatadah narrate, from Abu Nadrah, from Qays ibn Abbad, who said: I said to Ammar ibn Yasir: What of your fighting, is it an opinion you held, for opinion errs and is right, or a covenant the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made with you? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made no covenant with us that he did not make with all people. And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - Shubah said: and I think he said: Hudhayfah narrated to me, he said - : In my ummah there are twelve hypocrites who will not enter Paradise nor find its scent until the camel passes through the eye of the needle; eight of them the dubaylah will suffice against: a lamp of fire that appears in their shoulders until it pierces - or gushes - from their chests."
"1617","(1617): Sulayman al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hazawwar narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Maryam say: I heard Ammar ibn Yasir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The righteous are not adorned in this world with the like of renunciation of this world."
"1618","(1618): Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Salih narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Rashid, who said: Ammar spoke and was concise, and it was said to him: You have said something; if only you had added for us. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to shorten sermons."
"1619","(1619): Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Najiyah al-Anazi, who said: Ammar and Abd Allah ibn Masud began discussing tayammum. Abd Allah said: If I stayed a month in which I did not find water, I would not pray. Ammar said to him: Do you not remember when I and you were with the camels, and I became junub, and I rolled as an animal rolls, then when I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him what I had done, he said: Tayammum would have sufficed you."
"1620","(1620): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from Nuaym ibn Hanzalah, from Ammar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever is two-faced in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"1621","(1621): Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Salih narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, Abu Rashid narrated to us, who said: Ammar ibn Yasir addressed us and was brief in the sermon. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to lengthen the sermon."
"1622","(1622): Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabalah, Amr ibn al-Numan narrated to us, from Kathir Abu al-Fadl, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, who said: I heard Ammar ibn Yasir say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: What day is this? We said: The day of sacrifice. He said: What month is this? We said: Dhu al-Hijjah, a sacred month. He said: What city is this? We said: The sacred city. He said: Your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred like the sacredness of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this city of yours. Let the witness convey to the absent."
"1623","(1623): al-Salt ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Murrah narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Sulayman, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard Ammar ibn Yasir say: I was commanded to fight the oath-breakers, the unjust, and the renegades."
"1624","(1624): Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from his father, who said: I was with Ammar, and he would supplicate with a supplication in his prayer, then a man came to him, and Ammar said to him, say: O Allah, by Your knowledge of the unseen and Your power over creation, keep me alive as long as You know life is good for me, and take me when You know death is good for me. O Allah, I ask You for fear of You in secret and in public, and the word of truth in pleasure and anger, and moderation in wealth and poverty, and I ask You for contentment after decree, and coolness of life after death, and I ask You for longing to meet You without harmful adversity or misguiding trial. O Allah, adorn me with the adornment of faith, and make me of those who guide and are guided. Then he said: Shall I not teach you words better than them? As if raising them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: When you take your bed at night, say: O Allah, I have submitted myself to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, believed in Your revealed Book and Your sent Prophet. My soul is a soul You created; its life is Yours and its death is Yours. If You take it, have mercy on it, and if You delay it, guard it with the guarding of faith."
"1625","(1625): Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Ata, from Maysarah and Abu al-Bakhtari, that Ammar on the day of Siffin kept fighting and was not killed, then he would come to Ali and say: O Commander of the Believers, is this not the day of such and such? And he would say: Go away from you. He said that several times, then milk was brought and he drank it. Ammar said: This is the last drink I shall drink of this world. Then he advanced and fought until he was killed."
"1626","(1626): Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Salamah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, from Ammar ibn Yasir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of the fitrah are rinsing the mouth, inhaling water into the nose, trimming the mustache, the siwak, washing the knuckles, plucking the armpits, shaving the pubes, circumcision, and sprinkling water after urination."
"1627","(1627): Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim al-Juddi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Said ibn Abi Said, that Ammar prayed, and a man said to him: You have made the prayer light, O Abu al-Yaqzan. He said: Did you see me omit any of its limits? I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man prays, then leaves, and there is written for him only its half, its third, its fourth, its fifth, its sixth, its eighth, its ninth, its tenth."
"1628","(1628): Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Shair narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, from Ammar ibn Yasir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped at Dhat al-Jaysh with Aishah his wife, and a necklace of hers of Zafari onyx broke, so the people were held up seeking her necklace until dawn broke, and the people had no water with them. Abu Bakr became angry at her and said: You have held up the people while they have no water? So Allah sent down upon His Messenger the concession of purification with clean earth. The Muslims rose with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), struck their hands in the earth, raised their hands without taking any dust, and wiped their faces and hands with them up to the shoulders, and from the insides of their hands to the armpits."
"1629","(1629): Hajjaj narrated to us, Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abd Allah ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: I was among the people when the concession of wiping with earth when we do not find water was sent down. He said: We struck one strike with the hands on the earth for the face, and wiped it one wiping. He said: Then we struck another strike for the hands, and wiped them with it up to the shoulders, front and back."
"1630","(1630): Hajjaj narrated to us, Yaqub narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, that Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah informed him, from his father, from Ammar ibn Yasir, that he said: We wiped ourselves with dust with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), wiping our faces and hands up to the shoulders."
"1631","(1631): Hajjaj narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah, that Ammar ibn Yasir would narrate: that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey with Aishah, and her necklace was lost, so the people were held up seeking it while they had no water. Allah sent down the verse of tayammum. Ammar said: They struck their hands and wiped their faces with them, then returned and struck with their hands and wiped their hands with them up to the armpits, or he said: up to the shoulders. Abd al-Razzaq said: And Mamar would narrate, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah, that Ammar would wipe in tayammum his face one wiping, then return and wipe his hands up to the armpits, and Mamar would abbreviate it like this."
"1632","(1632): Hajjaj narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah on a journey, and a necklace of Aishah was lost, so they sought it until morning while the people had no water. The concession was sent down, and the Muslims rose and struck the earth with their hands and wiped their faces with them, and the outer and inner of their hands up to the armpits."
"1633","(1633): Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ammar, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and I greeted him, and he returned the greeting to me."
"1634","(1634): Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Ammar ibn Yasir, that he said: I came to my family at night from a journey with my hands cracked, and they scented me with saffron. I went in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting nor welcome me. He said: Go and wash this off yourself. So I went and washed it, then came and greeted him, and he returned the greeting and welcomed me, and said: The angels do not attend the funeral of a disbeliever with good, nor one scented with saffron, nor one junub; and he permitted one junub, when he wants to sleep, eat, or drink, to perform ablution."
"1635","(1635): Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ali ibn Abi Fatimah narrated to us, from Abu Maryam, who said: I heard Ammar ibn Yasir say: O Abu Musa, I adjure you by Allah, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire? So I ask you about a hadith; if you are truthful, well, otherwise I shall send against you one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who will make you affirm. Then I adjure you by Allah: did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not mean you yourself when he said: There will be a trial in my ummah; you, O Abu Musa, sleeping in it is better than sitting, and sitting better than standing, and standing better than walking; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) specified you and did not generalize the people? Abu Musa left without answering him anything."
"1636","(1636): Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Rukayn, from Ibn Hanzalah, from Ammar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is two-faced in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"1637","(1637): Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about tayammum? He commanded me with the face and the hands, one strike. And Qatadah would apply dust."
"1638","(1638): Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Yala ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from a son of Ammar, from Ammar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a single garment wrapped in it."
"1639","(1639): Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Najiyah, who said: Ammar said: I became junub while with the camels and found no water, so I rolled as an animal rolls. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him of that. He said: Tayammum would have sufficed you for that."
"1640","(1640): Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn al-Mughirah al-Shaybani, from one who told him, from the grandfather of his father al-Mukhariq, who said: I met Ammar ibn Yasir on the day of the Camel while he was urinating into a horn. I said to him: Shall I fight with you and be with you? He said: Fight under the banner of your people, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked a man to fight under the banner of his people."
"1641","(1641): Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar narrated to us, from his father, from Wasil ibn Hayyan, who said: Abu Wail said: Ammar ibn Yasir addressed us concisely and eloquently. When he descended, we said: O Abu al-Yaqzan, you were eloquent and concise; if only you had breathed (lengthened)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The length of a man's prayer and the shortness of his sermon is a sign of his understanding; so lengthen prayer and shorten sermons, and indeed some eloquence is magic."
"1642","(1642): Musa narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, who said: I heard Qays ibn Sad narrate, from Ata, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, from Ammar ibn Yasir, that he greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and he returned the greeting to him."
"1643","(1643): Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from Abu Ishaq, from Silah, who said: We were with Ammar on the day doubted of Ramadan, and a sheep was brought, and some people withdrew. Ammar said: Whoever fasts this day has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1644","(1644): Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: Umm Hasan said: The Mother of the Believers Umm Salamah said: I have not forgotten the day of the Trench when he was handing them milk while his hair was dusty, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he said: And Ammar came, and he said: Woe to you - Khalid doubted whether wayhaka or waylaka - son of Sumayyah, the rebellious party will kill you. Ibn Awn said: I narrated to Muhammad from his mother, and he said: She used to visit Umm Salamah."
"1645","(1645): Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, who said: I heard Abu Wail say: When Ali sent Ammar and al-Hasan to Kufah to rouse them, Ammar addressed and said: Indeed I know that she is his wife in this world and the Hereafter, meaning Aishah."
"1646","(1646): Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Yala ibn al-Harith, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from a son of Ammar, from Ammar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a garment."
"1647","(1647): Musa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Habib, from Abd Allah ibn Kathir, who said: Ammar ibn Yasir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to lengthen prayer and shorten the sermon."
"1648","(1648): Muhammad ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Umar ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, that Ammar ibn Yasir entered the mosque and prayed two light rakahs. A man said: You made them light, O Abu al-Yaqzan. He said: Did you see me omit any of its limits? I hastened with them against whispering; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man prays, and perhaps he has of his prayer only its tenth, ninth, eighth, seventh, sixth, fifth, fourth, third, or half."
"1649","(1649): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated to us, from Israil, from Simak, from Tharwan ibn Milhan, who said: We were sitting in the mosque when Ammar passed us. We said to him: Narrate to us the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the trial. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be after me rulers fighting over kingship, killing one another for it. We said: Had another than you narrated it to us, we would have disbelieved him; indeed it will be."
"1650","(1650): al-Hasan ibn Qazaah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Khilas ibn Amr, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Table was sent down from heaven, bread and meat, and they were commanded not to betray, nor store for tomorrow. They betrayed, stored, and lifted, so they were transformed into monkeys and pigs."
"1651","(1651): Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, that Ammar ibn Yasir said: We performed tayammum with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we wiped our faces and our hands up to the shoulders with dust."
"1652","(1652): Muhammad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, Sad ibn Ibrahim informed me, from one who informed him, from Ammar ibn Yasir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters; whoever avoids them, they are a protection for his religion, and whoever falls into them is about to fall into major sins, like one pasturing around a sanctuary about to fall into it; every king has a sanctuary."
"1653","Musnad of al-Bara ibn Azib (1654): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes to the desert becomes coarse."
"1654","(1655): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Zakariyya, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: We camped with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Hudaybiyah, and we found its water drunk up by the first people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat at the well, called for a bucket from it, took from it with his mouth, spat it into it, and supplicated to Allah. Its water increased until the people were satisfied from it."
"1655","(1656): Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Muammar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the kalalah, and he said: The summer verse suffices you."
"1656","(1657): Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath al-Nakhai narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: It was asked: Where would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate? He said: He would prostrate between his palms."
"1657","(1658): Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he began prayer, raise his hands until his thumbs were level with, or parallel to, his ears."
"1658","(1659): And from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a right upon Muslims that one of them bathe on Friday, and touch perfume if there is any with his family; if there is none with them, then water is perfume. Hushaym said: I said to Yazid: Is there bathing other than Friday? He said: Yes, the day of Fitr, the day of Adha, the day of Arafah, and Friday, and he said it therein."
"1659","(1660): Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Adhrami narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed umrah before hajj. He said: And Aishah said: He knew that he performed four umrahs of his umrah in the Farewell Pilgrimage."
"1660","(1661): Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the day of sacrifice and said: Let no one slaughter until he prays. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a day in which meat is disliked, and I hastened my sacrifice to feed my family and the people of my house, or my family and my neighbors. He said: You have done it, so repeat another slaughter. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a young milk goat better than two meat sheep; shall I slaughter it? He said: Yes, and it is better than your sacrifice, but no young goat will suffice for anyone after you."
"1661","(1662): Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Shabi, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the day of Adha after prayer and said: Whoever prays our prayer and offers our sacrifice has attained the sacrifice; whoever sacrifices before prayer, his sheep is a meat sheep with no sacrifice for him. Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, the uncle of al-Bara, said: O Messenger of Allah, I sacrificed my sheep before prayer, knowing the day is a day of eating and drinking, and I wished my sheep to be the first thing slaughtered in my house, so I slaughtered my sheep and ate before coming to prayer. He said: Your sheep is a meat sheep. He said: O Messenger of Allah, we have a young goat dearer to me than two sheep; will it suffice me? He said: Yes, but it will never suffice anyone after you."
"1662","(1663): Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Fitr, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on a journey, he would say: O Allah, a conveyance conveying good, forgiveness from You and pleasure; in Your hand is good; You are over all things capable. O Allah, You are the companion in travel and the successor over family. O Allah, ease travel for us and fold the earth for us. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardship of travel and the gloom of return."
"1663","(1664): Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Bahz narrated to me, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Rabi ibn al-Bara, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he returned from a journey, would say: Returning, repenting, worshipping, praising our Lord."
"1664","(1665): Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Bahz narrated to me, Shubah narrated to us, Adi ibn Thabit narrated to me, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and recited in the last Isha in one of the two rakahs with 'By the fig and the olive.'"
"1665","(1666): Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ashath informed us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent my uncle to a man who married his father's wife, ordering him to strike his neck."
"1666","(1667): Abu Mamar narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Ashath, from Adi, from al-Bara: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man to one who married his father's wife, ordering him to strike his neck and bring his head."
"1667","(1668): Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman and Abu Dawud narrated to us, both saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Sad ibn Ubaydah narrate, from al-Bara, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a man, when he takes his bed, to say: O Allah, I have submitted myself to You, turned my face to You, leaned my back upon You, entrusted my affair to You, in hope and fear of You; there is no refuge nor escape from You except to You; I believe in Your Book which You sent down, and in Your Messenger whom You sent. If he dies, he dies upon the fitrah."
"1668","(1669): Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would place his face between his palms when he prostrated."
"1669","(1670): Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Qanan ibn Abd Allah al-Nahmi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard Abu Musa reciting, and said: As if the voice of this one is from the flutes of the family of Dawud."
"1670","(1671): Muhammad ibn Bakkar, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uqbah ibn Abi al-Ayzar narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Bara, who said: We prostrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Zuhr, and we thought he recited 'The Revelation' of the prostration."
"1671","(1672): Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Bara, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions went out, and we entered ihram for hajj. When we came to Makkah, he said: Make your hajj an umrah. People said: O Messenger of Allah, we entered ihram for hajj; how do we make it an umrah? He said: See what I command you and do it. He said: They answered him back, so he became angry, then went until he entered upon Aishah angry. He said: She saw anger in his face and said: Who has angered you; may Allah be angry with him? He said: Why should I not be angry when I command a matter and it is not followed?"
"1672","(1673): Khalid ibn Mirdas narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Zayd ibn Abi al-Shatha al-Abdi, from al-Bara, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two Muslims meet, shake hands, praise Allah, and seek His forgiveness, they are forgiven."
"1673","(1674): Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut in Maghrib and Fajr prayer. Amr said: I mentioned that to Ibrahim, and he became angry and said: He was a man of authority, meaning Ibn Abi Layla."
"1674","(1675): Ibrahim ibn Dinar narrated to us, Musab ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Hamzah ibn Habib al-Zayyat, from Abu Ishaq al-Sabii, from al-Bara, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us until he made the secluded maidens in their houses - or he said: in their chambers - hear, and said: O company of those who believed with their tongues, do not backbite Muslims nor follow their faults; for whoever follows his brother's fault, Allah follows his fault, and whomever Allah follows in his fault, He exposes him in the midst of his house."
"1675","(1676): Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, that Muharib ibn Dithar told him, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Yazid say on the pulpit: al-Bara ibn Azib narrated to us that they would pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he bowed they bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing and said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, we remained standing until we saw him place (his forehead)."
"1676","(1677): Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Awwam, Azrah ibn al-Harith al-Shaybani informed me, from al-Bara, who said: When we prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and raised our heads from bowing, we stood in rows until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, then we followed him."
"1677","(1678): Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he met the idolaters on the day of Hunayn, dismounted from his mule and stood on the ground."
"1678","(1679): Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Hafsah bint Azib, from al-Bara, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him about prayer times? He commanded Bilal, who advanced and delayed, and said: The time is between them."
"1679","(1680): Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Utaybah informed me, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated to me, narrating from al-Bara, who said: The bowing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he raised his head from bowing, and when he prostrated, and between the two prostrations, were nearly equal."
"1680","(1681): And Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla narrate, from al-Bara, who said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he bowed, when he raised his head from bowing, when he prostrated, and when he raised his head from the two prostrations, was nearly equal."
"1681","(1682): Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, Yunus ibn Amr narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah, from his father Abd Allah ibn Masud, that he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lay down to sleep, he placed his right hand under his right cheek and said: O Allah, guard me from Your punishment on the day You gather Your servants."
"1682","(1683): Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Yunus ibn Amr narrated to us, who said: My father said: al-Bara ibn Azib narrated to us, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like, except that he said: on the day You resurrect Your servants."
"1683","(1684): Ibrahim ibn Ararah ibn al-Birind narrated to us, Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, Masud ibn Sad narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a right upon Muslims to bathe on Friday."
"1684","(1685): Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Awf, from Abu Abd Allah Maymun, from al-Bara, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded digging the Trench. He said: A rock appeared to us that pickaxes would not take, so they complained of that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He took the pickaxe - and I think he said: and put down his garment - struck a blow and said: In the name of Allah, breaking a third of the rock. Then he said: Allah is Greatest, I have been given the keys of Syria; indeed I see its red palaces from this place of mine. Then he said: In the name of Allah, and struck another, breaking its third, and said: Allah is Greatest, I have been given the keys of Persia; by Allah, indeed I see al-Madain and its white palace from this place of mine. Then he said: In the name of Allah, and struck another, breaking the rest of the stone, and said: Allah is Greatest, I have been given the keys of Yemen; by Allah, indeed I see the keys of Sanaa from this place of mine."
"1685","(1686): Khalid ibn Mirdas narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Abi Hakim, from Talhah ibn Nafi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beautify the Quran with your voices."
"1686","(1687): Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Qanan ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spread peace and you will be safe; and insolence is evil. Abu Muawiyah said: meaning much idle play."
"1687","(1688): Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us, Abu Ali Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever calls Madinah Yathrib, let him seek Allah's forgiveness."
"1688","(1689): Ishaq narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Isa, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he began prayer, would raise his hands, then not raise them until he finished."
"1689","(1690): Ishaq narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began prayer, he would raise his hands toward his head, then not repeat."
"1690","(1691): Ishaq narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he began prayer, say the takbir and raise his hands until they nearly faced his ears, then he did not repeat."
"1691","(1692): Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, who said: I heard Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands when he faced prayer, until I saw his thumbs near his ears, then he did not raise them."
"1692","(1693): Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hudayj ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fifteen campaigns."
"1693","(1694): He said: And I heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) some ten campaigns."
"1694","(1695): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: I and Ibn Umar were presented on the day of Badr to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he deemed us small, and we witnessed the day of Uhud."
"1695","(1696): Abu Bakr narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Shabi, from al-Bara, who said: Ibrahim the son of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died at sixteen months, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bury him in al-Baqi, for he has a nursing mother completing his nursing in Paradise."
"1696","(1697): al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, al-Bara ibn Azib narrated to us - and he was not untruthful - who said: We would pray behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, none of us bent his back until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his forehead on the ground, then when he placed his forehead on the ground we fell in prostration."
"1697","(1698): Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us while our pots boiled with donkey meat, and he ordered us to overturn them, so we overturned them."
"1698","(1699): And from al-Bara, who said: We never saw anyone in a red suit, combed, more handsome than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he had hair near his shoulders."
"1699","(1700): Zakariyya narrated to us, Abu Waki narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: I never saw one with locks in a suit more handsome than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1700","(1701): Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began prayer, he would raise his hands until he faced his ears with them. I mentioned that to Adi ibn Thabit, and he said: I heard al-Bara mention that."
"1701","(1702): Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, who said: Abu Yaqub al-Thaqafi narrated to me, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, freedman of Muhammad ibn al-Qasim, who said: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim sent me to al-Bara ibn Azib to ask him about the banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what it was? He said: It was black, square, of namirah cloth."
"1702","(1703): Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: Of what they stipulated upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was that they enter Makkah only with julubban al-silah. He said: And what is julubban al-silah? He said: The quiver and what is in it."
"1703","(1704): Jafar ibn Humayd al-Kufi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad narrated to us, from his father, from al-Bara, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How do you speak of the joy of a man whose camel escapes from him dragging its rein in a barren land with no food or drink in it, with his food and drink upon it, and he seeks it until it distresses him, then it passes by the stump of a tree, its rein catches, and he finds it caught to it? We said: Greatly, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than the man with his camel."
"1704","(1705): Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: I never saw anyone in a red suit more handsome than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), combed; he had hair near his ears, or he said: his shoulders - the doubt is from Muhriz."
"1705","(1706): Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal, al-Hasan ibn Umarah, and Fitr narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Beautify the Quran with your voices."
"1706","(1707): Jafar ibn Humayd al-Kufi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad narrated to us, from his father, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you prostrate, place your palms and raise your elbows."
"1707","(1708): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Abu Raja al-Khurasani Abd Allah ibn Waqid, from Muhammad ibn Malik, who said: I saw on al-Bara a gold ring, and he was questioned about it. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed, and this ring remained. He said: Whom do you see most deserving of it? Then he said: Come near, O Bara. He put it on my finger and said: Wear what Allah and His Messenger have clothed you."
"1708","(1709): Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, who said: Sheep are blessing."
"1709","(1710): Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, who said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from Makkah to Madinah, Suraqah ibn Jushum followed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against him, and his horse sank with him. He said: Supplicate to Allah for me and I will not harm you. So he supplicated for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thirsted, and they passed a shepherd. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: I took a cup and milked into it a portion of milk, brought it to him, and he drank, then drank until I was pleased."
"1710","(1711-1712): Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah and another man, from al-Bara, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to sleep, he pillowed his right side and said: O Allah, guard me from Your punishment on the day You gather Your servants. Shubah said: Abu Ishaq said: And Abu al-Ahwas said: on the day You resurrect Your servants."
"1711","(1713): Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard al-Bara say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made peace with the people of Makkah, Ali wrote a document between them, writing: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. The idolaters said: Do not write Muhammad, Messenger of Allah; had you been the Messenger of Allah we would not have fought you. He said to Ali: Erase it. Ali said: I am not one to erase it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) erased it with his hand, and made peace with them that he and his companions enter it three days, entering it only with julubban al-silah. They asked him: What is julubban al-silah? He said: The quiver and what is in it."
"1712","(1714): He said: And I heard Abu Ishaq say: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a man of medium stature, wide between the shoulders, with a great mass of hair to his earlobes, upon him a red suit; I never saw anything at all more handsome than him."
"1713","(1715): And with his chain, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: The first of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to come was Musab ibn Umayr and Ibn Umm Maktum; they would teach the people. He said: Then Bilal, Sad, and Ammar ibn Yasir came. He said: Then Umar ibn al-Khattab came with twenty of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and I never saw the people of Madinah rejoice at anything as they rejoiced at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Until the slave girls would say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come. He said: He did not come until I had recited 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,' among suwar of the Mufassal."
"1714","(1716): And with his chain, who said: I heard al-Bara say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would carry earth, and the earth indeed covered his belly, while he said - and perhaps he said: raising his voice with it."
"1715","(1717): And with his chain, from al-Bara, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people sitting in the road and said: If you must do it, guide the way, return greeting, and aid the oppressed."
"1716","(1718): Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like. Shubah said: I said to Abu Ishaq: Did you hear it from al-Bara? He said: No."
"1717","(1719): Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: al-Bara ibn Azib said: People of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while drinking wine. When its prohibition was sent down, people of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What of our companions who died while drinking it? Then was sent down: 'There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted, when they fear and believe.'"
"1718","(1720): Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, the like. Shubah said: I said: Did you hear it from al-Bara? He said: No."
"1719","(1721): Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, that he heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a man, when he takes his bed, to say: O Allah, I have submitted myself to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, leaned my back upon You, in hope and fear of You; there is no refuge nor escape from You except to You; I believe in Your Book which You sent down, and in Your Prophet whom You sent. If he dies, he dies upon the fitrah."
"1720","(1722): And with it, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard al-Bara say: A man recited al-Kahf while there was an animal in the house, and it began to shy. He gave greeting, and behold a mist or cloud had covered him. He mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Recite, O so-and-so, for it is tranquillity that descended at the Quran, or descended for the Quran."
"1721","(1723): And with it, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard al-Bara say: The last verse sent down was the kalalah, and the last surah sent down was Baraah."
"1722","(1724): And with it, from Abu Ishaq, that he heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: I was deemed small on the day of Badr, I and Ibn Umar; the Emigrants were somewhat over sixty, and the Ansar somewhat over two hundred and forty."
"1723","(1725): And with his chain, from Abu Ishaq, that he heard al-Bara say concerning this verse: 'Not equal are those who sit among the believers, other than those of harm, and those who strive in the way of Allah.' He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Zayd, and he brought a shoulder blade. He said: Ibn Umm Maktum complained of his blindness, so was sent down: 'Not equal are those who sit among the believers, other than those of harm.'"
"1724","(1726): Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from a man, from Zayd ibn Thabit, concerning this verse 'Not equal are those who sit,' the like of the hadith of al-Bara."
"1725","(1727): Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard al-Bara, when a man of Qays asked him, saying: Did you flee from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn? Al-Bara said: But the Messenger of Allah did not flee. Hawazin were archers, and when we charged upon them and we bent over the spoils, they faced us with arrows. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon his white mule, with Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith holding its bridle, saying: I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib."
"1726","(1728): Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: al-Bara said: We obtained donkeys on the day of Khaybar, and the crier of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out: Overturn the pots."
"1727","(1729): Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard al-Rabi ibn al-Bara say: I heard al-Bara say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from a journey, he would say: Returning, worshipping, praising our Lord."
"1728","(1730): And with his chain, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard al-Bara say: A silk suit was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his companions began touching it, marveling at its softness. He said: Do you marvel at the softness of this? The handkerchiefs of Sad in Paradise are better than it and softer."
"1729","(1731): Muhammad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara, who said: A silk suit was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his companions began touching it. He said: Do you marvel at the softness of this? The handkerchiefs of Sad in Paradise are softer than this."
"1730","(1732): Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard al-Bara say: The Ansar, when they performed hajj, would not enter houses except from their backs. A man of the Ansar came and entered through his door, and he was spoken to of that, so was sent down: 'And righteousness is not that you come houses from their backs,' the verse."
"1731","(1733): Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Qanan ibn Abd Allah al-Nahmi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he heard Abu Musa reciting the Quran: As if the voice of this one is from the voices of the family of Dawud."
"1732","Musnad of Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani (1734): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Muawwidhatayn? Uqbah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us with them in Fajr prayer, then called me and I mentioned his hadith about them."
"1733","(1735): Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abd Allah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Recite these two verses of the end of Surat al-Baqarah; I was given them from beneath the Throne."
"1734","(1736): Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: While I was leading the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a mountain pass of those passes, he said: O Uqab, will you not ride? I deemed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) too exalted for me to ride his mount. Then he said: O Uqab, will you not ride? I feared it would be disobedience, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted and I rode a while, then he rode. Then he said: O Uqab, shall I not teach you two surahs of the best surahs people recited? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He taught me: Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the dawn, and Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind. Then prayer was established, and the Messenger of Allah advanced and recited them, then passed by me and said: How did you see, O Uqab? Recite them whenever you sleep and rise."
"1735","(1737): Zuhayr narrated to us, Man ibn Isa narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One secret with the Quran is like one secret with charity, and one open with the Quran is like one open with charity."
"1736","(1738): Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Qari narrated to us, who said: My uncle Iyas ibn Amir narrated to me, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: When was sent down: 'So glorify the name of your Lord, the Great,' the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Put it in your bowing. When was sent down: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,' he said: Put it in your prostration."
"1737","(1739): Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Amr informed me, that Shuayb ibn Zarah told him, who said: Uqbah ibn Amir narrated to me, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to his companions: Do not frighten yourselves, or he said: souls. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we frighten ourselves? He said: By debt."
"1738","(1740): Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Qabath ibn Razin al-Misri narrated to us, who said: I heard Ulayy ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi say: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani say: We were sitting in the mosque reciting the Quran, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us and said: Learn the Book of Allah and spread it. Qabath said: I think he said: And chant it melodiously, for by Him in whose hand is my soul, it is more fleeting than milch camels from hobbles."
"1739","(1741): Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Bakr ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ulayy, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not force your sick to food and drink, for Allah feeds them and gives them drink."
"1740","(1742): Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu Ali, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Lands will be opened to you, and Allah will suffice you, so let none of you fail to amuse himself with his arrows."
"1741","Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu Ali Thumama ibn Shafi, that he heard Uqba ibn Amir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on the pulpit saying: And prepare for them whatever you can of strength. Verily strength is archery, verily strength is archery, verily strength is archery."
"1742","Abu Yahya Kamil ibn Talha narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Ka'b ibn Alqama narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasa al-Mahri, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqba ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A vow is an oath, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"1743","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an al-Ma'afiri, from Uqba ibn Amir al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the Qur'an were placed in a leather skin and then cast into the Fire, it would not burn. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He explained it as: whoever memorizes the Qur'an and then enters the Fire is worse than a pig."
"1744","Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, he said: Abu Qabil Huyayy ibn Hani al-Ma'afiri narrated to me, he said: I heard Uqba ibn Amir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The destruction of my community lies in the Book and milk. They said: What are the Book and milk? He said: They learn the Qur'an and interpret it contrary to its true interpretation, and they love milk so they abandon the congregations and Friday prayers and go out to the desert."
"1745","Abu Abdullah al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, he said: Abu Qabil al-Ma'afiri narrated to me, from Abu Ushshana al-Ma'afiri, from Uqba ibn Amir al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever leaves his house for the mosque, ten good deeds are recorded for him for every step he takes, and the one who sits in the mosque waiting for the prayer is like the devout worshipper, and he is recorded among those praying until he returns to his house."
"1746","Kamil ibn Talha narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqba, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over those killed at Uhud after eight years, like one bidding farewell to the living and the dead, and said: There are predecessors before you, and I am a witness over you, and your appointment is the Pond, and I am looking at it from this place of mine, and its width is like the distance between Ayla and al-Juhfa, and I was given the keys of the treasures of the earth while I am in this station of mine, and I do not fear for you that you will associate partners with Allah, but I fear for you the world, that you will compete over it. Uqba said: That was the last look I ever cast at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1747","Kamil narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Abu Ushshana narrated to us, he said: I heard Uqba ibn Amir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Our Lord marvels at the young man who has no youthful recklessness."
"1748","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Za'ida, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Uqba ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on the guard who keeps watch."
"1749","Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr informed, that Hisham ibn Abi Ruqayya narrated to him, he said: I heard Maslama ibn Mukhallad, while he stood on the pulpit delivering a sermon, saying: O people, do you not have in coarse cotton and linen what suffices you instead of silk? And here is a man among you who reports from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Stand, O Uqba. So Uqba ibn Amir stood, and I was listening, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. And I bear witness that I heard him say: Whoever wears silk in this world will be deprived of wearing it in the Hereafter."
"1750","Ahmad ibn Isa al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn Malik, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Ja'far ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hakam, who said: I heard Uqba ibn Amir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is thrown from his mount in the path of Allah and dies is a martyr."
"1751","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Yahya, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr narrated to me, that Abu Sa'id informed him, that Abdullah ibn Malik informed him, that Uqba ibn Amir informed him, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about his sister who vowed to walk wearing a head cover. So he ordered her to wear the head cover, to ride, and to fast three days."
"1752","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far al-Ansari narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani, from Uqba ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those by which private parts are made lawful."
"1753","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to us, from his father, who said: I heard Uqba ibn Amir say: There are three hours in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid us to pray or to bury our dead: when the sun rises until it ascends, when the sun stands at midday until it declines, and when it inclines toward sunset until it sets."
"1754","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasa, from Uqba ibn Amir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The collector of tolls will not enter Paradise, meaning the tithe-taker."
"1755","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid informed us, from Qatada, from Nu'aym ibn Hammar, from Uqba ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Son of Adam, are you unable to pray four units at the beginning of the day so that I suffice you for the rest of your day?"
"1756","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwa'i informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ba'ja al-Juhani, from Uqba ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sacrificial animals, and a young goat fell to my share. I said: O Messenger of Allah, a young goat has fallen to my share. He said: Sacrifice it."
"1757","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Haywa ibn Shurayh, from Khalid ibn Ubayd, from Mishrah, from Uqba ibn Amir al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever hangs an amulet, may Allah not complete for him, and whoever hangs a cowrie shell, may Allah not grant him ease."
"1758","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Qays al-Judhami, from Uqba ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a believing slave, it will be his ransom from the Fire."
"1759","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Habban narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmala narrated to us, that a man from Alexandria of Hamdan called Abu Ali narrated to him, he said: We went out on a journey with Uqba ibn Amir, and we said to him: Lead us in prayer, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: I will not do it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever leads the people in prayer and gets the time right and completes the prayer, there is reward for him and for them, and whoever falls short in any of that, the burden is upon him and not upon them."
"1760","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasa al-Tujibi, from Uqba ibn Amir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It is not lawful for a Muslim man to propose over the proposal of his brother until he abandons it, nor to bargain over his bargain until he abandons it."
"1761","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywa narrated to us, Abu Aqil narrated to us, from his cousin, from Uqba ibn Amir, that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the expedition of Tabuk. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat one day narrating to his companions and said: Whoever stands when the sun rises before him, performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then stands and prays two units, his sins are forgiven, and he becomes as his mother bore him."
"1762","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Harmala ibn Imran narrated to us, from Abu Ushshana, from Uqba ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has three daughters and is patient with them, feeding them, giving them drink, and clothing them from his means, they will be a veil for him from the Fire."
"1763","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqba, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there is healing in anything, it is in the cut of a cupper, or a drink of honey, or a branding of fire that touches the ailment, and I dislike branding and do not love it."
"1764","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Harmala ibn Imran, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqba, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is in the shade of his charity until judgment is passed among the people, or he said: until requital is taken among the people. And Abu al-Khayr would not let a day pass without giving something in charity, even a cake or an onion."
"1765","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, Abu Amr Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Dhimari informed me, that he heard al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of Yazid ibn Mu'awiya ibn Abi Sufyan, raising the narration to Uqba, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance Hell from him by a journey of one hundred years."
"1766","Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Shayban narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, he said: I heard Ata ibn Rabah; Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to us: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing raisins with dates, and unripe dates with dates."
"1767","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to have drink prepared for him in a stone vessel."
"1768","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, al-Furat ibn Abi al-Furat al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrating, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I slept, then woke, then slept, then woke. Then a Muslim man stood and said: Prayer, prayer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with his head dripping, and he prayed, then said: Were it not that I would burden my community, and I do not like to burden my community, I would have loved for you to pray this prayer at this hour. Al-Furat said: I think it was the night prayer."
"1769","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Habib al-Mu'allim, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Restrain your wandering creatures until the fright of the night prayer departs, for it is an hour in which devils blaze about."
"1770","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to close the doors, to cover the vessels, to tie the waterskins, to extinguish the lamps, and to restrain our livestock until the darkness of the night prayer departs. And he forbade anyone to eat with his left hand, to walk in a single sandal, to wrap himself in a single garment without leaving an opening, and to sit wrapping the knees with a single garment."
"1771","Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the Negus. He said: I was in the second row, or the third."
"1772","Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, and from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra: that a man called Abu Humayd brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a vessel containing milk from al-Naqi' in the daytime, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you not cover it, even by placing a stick across it?"
"1773","Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright and draw near, and none of you will be saved by his deeds. We said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me with mercy from Him."
"1774","al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Isa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, that Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shame and disgrace will so overwhelm the son of Adam on the Day of Resurrection at the standing before Allah that the servant will wish to be ordered into the Fire."
"1775","Shayban narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sulayman ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) summoned Abu Tayba and had him cup him, then asked about his fee. He said: Three measures. He said: So he remitted one measure from him."
"1776","Shayban narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sulayman ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought Muharib and Khasafa at Nakhl. They saw an unguarded moment among the Muslims, so a man of theirs called Gawrath ibn al-Harith came until he stood over the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a sword and said: Who will protect you from me? He said: Allah. So the sword fell from his hand, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the sword and said to him: Who will protect you from me? He said: Be the best of takers. He said: Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah? He said: No, but I pledge to you that I will not fight you, nor be with a people who fight you. So he let him go, and he came to his companions and said: I have come to you from the best of people. Then when it was noon or afternoon, the Prophet ordered the fear prayer, Abu Awana doubted. He said: The people were in two groups: a group facing their enemy, and a group praying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He prayed two units with the group that was with him, then they left and took the place of the others, and the others came and prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two units. So it was four units for the Messenger of Allah and two units for the people."
"1777","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that a man slaughtered a young male goat before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will not suffice for anyone after you to slaughter before praying."
"1778","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled in Ramadan, and fasting bore heavily upon a man of his companions, and his she-camel kept wandering with him beneath the shade of trees. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed, so he ordered him and he broke his fast. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a vessel of water and placed it on his hand, and when the people saw him drink, they drank."
"1779","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Wasi' ibn Habban, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted sharecropping of unripe dates for one, two, three, or four measures, and said: In every harvest there are ten measures, and what remains in clusters is placed in the mosque for the poor. Muhammad said: Today they stipulate that upon the merchants."
"1780","Suwayd narrated to us, from Malik, from Hashim ibn Hashim ibn Utba ibn Abi Waqqas, from Abdullah ibn Nistas, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a sinful oath upon this pulpit of mine will take his seat in the Fire."
"1781","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between a servant and disbelief is the abandonment of prayer."
"1782","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my pulpit and my chamber is a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon a canal of the canals of Paradise."
"1783","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Mu'alla, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought the repentance of a man who apostatized from Islam four times."
"1784","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: that they were on one of their expeditions and were struck by severe hunger, so the sea cast up a huge creature, and they ate from it for twenty-five days, fresh meat. Abu al-Zubayr said, Jabir ibn Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you brought us any of it?"
"1785","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that they slaughtered horses, mules, and domestic donkeys on the day of Khaybar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mules and donkeys, but did not forbid horses."
"1786","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gourds, varnished vessels, and hollowed stumps. Abu al-Zubayr said: Whenever Jabir could not find a waterskin, drink would be prepared for him in a stone vessel."
"1787","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion, no evil omen, no Safar, and no ghoul."
"1788","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar came to us, and we fed them ripe dates and gave them water to drink. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is part of the bliss about which you will be asked."
"1789","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man retires to his bed, an angel and a devil hasten to him. The angel says: Seal with good, and the devil says: Seal with evil. If he remembers Allah and then sleeps, the angel spends the night guarding him. When he wakes, the angel says: Open with good, and the devil says: Open with evil. If he says: Praise be to Allah who returned my soul to me and did not take it in my sleep, praise be to Allah who holds the heavens and the earth lest they cease, to the end of the verse, praise be to Allah who holds the sky lest it fall upon the earth except by His permission, then if he falls from his bed and dies, he enters Paradise."
"1790","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought two horned, white-black, large, castrated rams. He laid one down and said: In the name of Allah, and Allah is Greatest. O Allah, on behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad. Then he laid the other down and said: In the name of Allah, and Allah is Greatest, on behalf of Muhammad and his community: those who bore witness to You of oneness, and bore witness to me of conveyance."
"1791","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him during the expedition of Tabuk while he was on a red camel and the camel lagged behind: What is wrong with you, O Jabir? I said: O Messenger of Allah, my camel has lagged. He came to it from its rear, supplicated for it and urged it on. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) caught up with me and said: What happened to the camel, O Jabir? I said: O Messenger of Allah, it has kept ahead of us since last night. He said: For how much did you take it? I said: For thirteen dinars. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sell it to me for the price you took it for, and its back is yours until Medina. So I did. When we arrived in Medina, I haltered it and brought it to him, and he gave me the camel and the thirteen dinars."
"1792","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Bishr ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Umar ibn Nabhan, from Abu Shaddad, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things: whoever brings them along with faith will enter through whichever gate of Paradise he wishes, and will be married to the wide-eyed maidens wherever he wishes: whoever pardons his killer, whoever pays a hidden debt, and whoever recites Say: He is Allah, the One ten times after every prescribed prayer. Abu Bakr said: Or one of them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Or one of them."
"1793","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Isa ibn Jariya, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: Ubayy led the people in prayer in Quba, and an Ansari youth who had irrigation work entered his prayer. When he heard Ubayy reciting a long surah, he broke off his prayer. When Ubayy finished, he was told of that. Ubayy realized the youth was complaining to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the youth came close complaining about Ubayy. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some of you drive people away. When you pray, be brief, or he said: make it short. For behind you are the elderly, the sick, and those with needs."
"1794","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Isa ibn Jariya, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in Mecca and passed a man standing praying upon a rock. He went to the outskirts of Mecca and stayed a while, then returned and found the man still praying in the same state. He joined his hands and said three times: O people, upon you is moderation, upon you is moderation, upon you is moderation, for Allah will not tire until you tire."
"1795","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, Isa ibn Jariya narrated to us, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed in Mecca by a man praying upon a rock. He went to a side and stayed a while, then left and found the man still praying as before. He stood, joined his hands, and said: O people, upon you is moderation, upon you is moderation, for Allah does not tire until you tire."
"1796","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, Isa ibn Jariya informed us, from Jabir, who said: Ubayy used to lead the people of Quba in prayer. He began a long surah, and an Ansari youth joined him in prayer. When he heard him begin a long surah, the youth broke off his prayer, for he wanted to treat a water-carrying camel of his. When Ubayy ibn Ka'b finished, the people told him: So-and-so broke off the prayer. Ubayy became angry and went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining about the youth, and the youth came complaining about him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry until anger was seen on his face, then said: Some of you drive people away. When you pray, be brief, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, the sick, and those with needs."
"1797","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, Isa ibn Jariya narrated to me, from Jabir, who said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon. He sat beside Ubayy ibn Ka'b and asked him about something, but Ubayy did not answer him. Ibn Mas'ud thought it was resentment. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, Ibn Mas'ud said: O Ubayy, what prevented you from answering me? He said: You did not attend Friday with us. He said: Why? He said: You spoke while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon. Ibn Mas'ud went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ubayy spoke the truth. Obey Ubayy."
"1798","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, Isa ibn Jariya informed us, from Jabir, who said: Ibn Mas'ud entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, and he mentioned a narration similar to the hadith of Abd al-A'la."
"1799","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, from Isa ibn Jariya, Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, who said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, something happened with me last night, meaning in Ramadan. He said: What was it, O Ubayy? He said: Women in my house said: We do not recite the Qur'an, so we pray with your prayer. So I prayed eight units with them, then prayed witr. He said: It was like approval, and he said nothing."
"1800","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, Isa informed us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer in the month of Ramadan, eight units, and prayed witr. The next year we gathered in the mosque hoping he would come out to us, and we remained there until morning. Then we went in and said: O Messenger of Allah, we gathered in the mosque hoping you would lead us in prayer. He said: I feared, or disliked, that it would be made obligatory upon you."
